window.KB4IT_INDEX = [{"u":"ab.html","t":"ab","s":"from (a time)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag ab neun Uhr kommen die Handwerker. :: On Saturday from nine o'clock the workmen are coming."]]},{"u":"aber.html","t":"aber","s":"but","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schön, aber anstrengend. :: Nice, but tiring. Ich will spielen, aber ich muss Hausaufgaben machen. :: I want to play, but I have to do homework."]]},{"u":"abgeben.html","t":"abgeben","s":"to hand in / to leave with someone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Paketbote hat es bei mir abgegeben. :: The delivery man left it with me."]]},{"u":"abgemacht.html","t":"Abgemacht!","s":"Deal!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Gut, abgemacht! :: OK, it's a deal! Ist das abgemacht? :: Is that agreed?"],["usage","Usage","When you agree on a plan, such as who drives to training."]]},{"u":"abholen.html","t":"abholen","s":"to pick up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I will pick her up at quarter past four. Wer hat die Kinder abgeholt? :: Who picked up the children?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich abhole meine Tochter. :: Ich hole meine Tochter ab."]]},{"u":"abnahme.html","t":"Abnahme","s":"acceptance (of finished work)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Laufzeit beträgt 15 Jahre beginnend mit dem Monat, der auf die Abnahme der Anlage folgt. :: The term is 15 years, starting with the month after the acceptance of the system. Über die Abnahme ist ein Protokoll zu erstellen. :: A record must be made of the acceptance. Nach der Abnahme bekommen wir die Rechnung. :: After the acceptance we get the invoice."],["notes","Notes","After building work, the customer checks the result and signs that it is accepted: that is the Abnahme . Payments and the warranty usually start from that day. In other contexts Abnahme means a decrease, such as weight loss ( abnehmen : to lose weight)."]]},{"u":"absage-training-wegen-hitze.html","t":"Absage: Training wegen Hitze","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Hallo, ich wollte kurz Bescheid geben, dass Kind A. heute leider nicht zum Training kommen kann. :: Hello, I just wanted to let you know that child A. sadly cannot come to training today. ich: Bei den hohen Temperaturen möchte ich ihn lieber nicht trainieren lassen, auch wenn er sich riesig darauf gefreut hat. :: With these high temperatures I would rather not let him train, even though he was really looking forward to it. ich: Ich hoffe auf euer Verständnis. Vielen Dank und liebe Grüße! :: I hope you understand. Many thanks and best wishes! Trainer: Hallo, ist ok. Wir machen heute nur lockere Übungen. :: Hello, that's OK. Today we are only doing light exercises. ich: Danke! Beim nächsten Training ist er wieder dabei. :: Thanks! He'll be there again at the next training."],["variations","Variations","1 ich: Hallo, Kind A. kann heute wegen der großen Hitze nicht zum Training kommen. :: Hello, child A. cannot come to training today because of the great heat. 4 Trainer: Schade, aber verständlich. Bis zum nächsten Mal! :: A pity, but understandable. See you next time!"],["notes","Notes","Turns 1 to 3 follow the message drafted for the learner; the coach's real answer is in the text Antwort des Trainers: Training bei Hitze . sich freuen auf (+ Akkusativ) is about something in the future: Er freut sich auf das Training. sich freuen über is about something that already happened."]]},{"u":"ach.html","t":"ach","s":"oh","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ach so, jetzt verstehe ich. :: Oh I see, now I understand."]]},{"u":"acht.html","t":"acht","s":"eight","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist acht Uhr. Zeit fürs Bett! :: It's eight o'clock. Time for bed!"]]},{"u":"achten.html","t":"achten","s":"to pay attention to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Achten Sie bitte auf den Verkehr. :: Please watch the traffic. Achten Sie auf absterbende oder lose Baumteile. :: Watch out for dying or loose parts of trees."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Achten Sie den Verkehr. :: Achten Sie auf den Verkehr."],["notes","Notes","Without auf , jemanden achten means to respect someone. Achtung! on a sign comes from the same verb."]]},{"u":"achtung-liebe-wanderer.html","t":"Achtung! Liebe Wanderer","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Achtung! Liebe Wanderer, der Wanderweg quert hier eine stark befahrene Straße oder verläuft seitlich an dieser entlang. Leider wird hier oft sehr schnell gefahren. Achten Sie bitte auf den Verkehr und überqueren Sie die Straße möglichst zügig und auf direktem Weg. \"Der Sinn des Reisens ist es, an ein Ziel zu kommen, der Sinn des Wanderns, unterwegs zu sein.\" (Theodor Heuss) Deutsch-Luxemburgische Tourist-Information, Tel. [Telefon], [Website]"],["meaning","Meaning","Attention! Dear hikers, here the trail crosses a busy road or runs along its side. Sadly, people often drive very fast here. Please watch the traffic and cross the road as quickly as possible and straight across. The quote by Theodor Heuss, the first Federal President: the point of travelling is to arrive somewhere, the point of hiking is to be on the way. wird ... gefahren is a passive without a subject: it says that driving happens, not who drives."]]},{"u":"adjektivendungen.html","t":"Adjektivendungen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","An adjective after the noun has no ending: Der Ball ist . Before a noun it takes an ending, which depends on the article. neu After der, die, das (and dieser, jeder ): mostly -e , and -en in the Akkusativ masculine, in the Dativ and in the plural: der neu . e Ball, den neu en Ball, mit dem neu en Ball, die neu en Bälle After ein, kein, mein : the adjective shows the gender when the article does not: ein neu . er Ball, ein neu es Trikot, eine neu e Tasche With no article, the adjective takes the ending of der, die, das : warm . es Wasser, kalt e Milch"],["simple-german","Simple German","Vor dem Nomen hat das Adjektiv eine Endung: der kleine Sohn, ein kleiner Sohn, ein kleines Kind ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","ein neu Trikot :: ein neues Trikot mit dem neue Ball :: mit dem neuen Ball"]]},{"u":"akkusativ.html","t":"Akkusativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The Akkusativ is the case of the direct object: the person or thing the action goes to. Only the masculine article changes: der becomes den , ein becomes einen . Ich brauche einen Termin. Ich hole den Sohn ab. Hast du einen Ball? Verbs such as haben, brauchen, abholen, anrufen, besuchen and es gibt take the Akkusativ, and so do the prepositions für, ohne, um, gegen : für . den Trainer"],["simple-german","Simple German","Akkusativ: der wird den , ein wird einen . Ich brauche einen Termin. Nach für, ohne, um, gegen steht der Akkusativ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich brauche ein Termin. :: Ich brauche einen Termin. Das ist für der Trainer. :: Das ist für den Trainer."]]},{"u":"alles.html","t":"alles","s":"everything","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Trainer schreibt alles in den Chat. :: The coach writes everything in the chat. Heute ist alles voll. :: Everything is full today."],["notes","Notes","alle means everybody or all : Alle Kinder kommen mit."]]},{"u":"als.html","t":"als","s":"when (in the past) / than","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Als ich klein war, habe ich Handball gespielt. :: When I was little, I played handball. Die andere Mannschaft ist stärker als wir. :: The other team is stronger than us."],["notes","Notes","als for one moment in the past, wenn for the present, the future and repeated events. After a comparative, als means than ."]]},{"u":"alt.html","t":"alt","s":"old","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie alt ist dein Sohn? :: How old is your son? Ich bin 40 Jahre alt. :: I am 40 years old."],["notes","Notes","Age is said with sein and alt : Er ist acht Jahre alt."]]},{"u":"am-elternabend.html","t":"Am Elternabend","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Lehrerin: Guten Abend und herzlich willkommen! Schön, dass Sie alle da sind. :: Good evening and welcome! Nice that you are all here. Lehrerin: Im Dezember machen wir einen Ausflug ins Museum. Der Ausflug kostet fünf Euro. :: In December we are going on a trip to the museum. The trip costs five euros. ich: Entschuldigung, ich habe eine Frage. Wann kommen die Kinder zurück? :: Excuse me, I have a question. When do the children come back? Lehrerin: Um halb eins, also ganz normal. :: At half past twelve, so as usual. Vater: Müssen die Kinder etwas mitbringen? :: Do the children have to bring anything? Lehrerin: Ja, eine Brotdose, etwas zu trinken und warme Kleidung. :: Yes, a lunch box, something to drink and warm clothes. ich: Ich kann gern als Begleitung mitkommen. :: I'm happy to come along as a helper. Lehrerin: Wunderbar, vielen Dank! :: Wonderful, thank you very much!"],["variations","Variations","4 Lehrerin: Wir sind um zwölf Uhr zurück. Sie können die Kinder dann an der Schule abholen. :: We'll be back at twelve. You can pick up the children at school then."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Begleitung : a parent who goes along on a trip to help the teacher."]]},{"u":"am-montagetag-der-waermepumpe.html","t":"Am Montagetag der Wärmepumpe","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Monteur: Guten Morgen! Wir kommen wegen der Wärmepumpe. :: Good morning! We are here about the heat pump. ich: Guten Morgen! Kommen Sie herein. Der Heizungsraum ist im Keller. :: Good morning! Come in. The boiler room is in the basement. Monteur: Danke. Sind der Zählerschrank und die Heizkörper frei? :: Thank you. Are the meter cabinet and the radiators free? ich: Ja, wir haben alles frei geräumt. Wie lange dauert die Montage? :: Yes, we have cleared everything. How long does the installation take? Monteur: Zwei bis drei Tage. In dieser Zeit bleiben Heizung und Warmwasser kalt. :: Two to three days. During that time heating and hot water stay cold. ich: Alles klar. Wann machen wir die Abnahme? :: All right. When do we do the acceptance? Monteur: Am letzten Tag. Dann gehen wir alles zusammen durch, und Sie unterschreiben das Protokoll. :: On the last day. Then we go through everything together and you sign the record."],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Ja, alles ist frei. Brauchen Sie Strom oder Wasser von uns? :: Yes, everything is free. Do you need electricity or water from us? 5 Monteur: Heute stellen wir nur die Außeneinheit auf, morgen kommt der Rest. :: Today we only set up the outdoor unit; the rest comes tomorrow. 7 Monteur: Das macht die Bauleitung. Sie meldet sich bei Ihnen. :: The site manager does that. They will get in touch with you."],["notes","Notes","A model to practise before the installation day; it did not happen like this. frei räumen : to clear a space so the workers can reach it."]]},{"u":"an-schultagen-halteverbot.html","t":"An Schultagen Halteverbot","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","an Schultagen von 7-9h von 11-16h ausgenommen Linienbusse"],["meaning","Meaning","Three signs on one pole: The red triangle with two children: watch out, children (a school is near). The blue sign with a red cross: absolute no stopping ( absolutes Halteverbot ). You may not even stop for a moment. The arrow shows the direction in which the ban applies from the sign. The extra plate ( Zusatzzeichen ): the ban only applies on school days, from 7 to 9 and from 11 to 16 o'clock. Scheduled public buses ( Linienbusse ) are allowed to stop."]]},{"u":"an.html","t":"an","s":"at / on","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Treffpunkt ist um neun Uhr am Vereinsheim. :: The meeting point is at nine o'clock at the clubhouse."],["notes","Notes","am is an dem . Days take am : am Montag ."]]},{"u":"anfangen.html","t":"anfangen","s":"to begin / to start","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Weißt du, wann der Elternabend anfängt? :: Do you know when the parents' evening starts? Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. :: We start at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"anmeldung.html","t":"Anmeldung","s":"registration, sign-up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zur Anmeldung: Der Preis wird per Überweisung bezahlt. :: About registration: the price is paid by bank transfer. Die Überweisung gilt als verbindliche Anmeldung. :: The transfer counts as a binding registration."],["notes","Notes","verbindlich means binding: once you have signed up, you have to pay."]]},{"u":"anruf-im-sekretariat.html","t":"Anruf im Sekretariat","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Sekretärin: Grundschule, Sekretariat, guten Morgen. :: Primary school, office, good morning. ich: Guten Morgen. Hier ist Familie B. Meine Tochter geht in die Klasse 2b. :: Good morning. This is the B. family. My daughter is in class 2b. Sekretärin: Ja, was kann ich für Sie tun? :: Yes, what can I do for you? ich: Meine Tochter ist krank. Sie hat Fieber und bleibt heute zu Hause. :: My daughter is ill. She has a temperature and is staying at home today. Sekretärin: Oh, gute Besserung! Wie lange bleibt sie zu Hause? :: Oh, get well soon! How long will she stay at home? ich: Ich weiß es noch nicht. Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: I don't know yet. We are going to the paediatrician today. Sekretärin: Gut. Bitte rufen Sie wieder an, wenn sie länger krank ist. :: All right. Please call again if she is ill for longer. ich: Ja, mache ich. Auf Wiederhören! :: Yes, I will. Goodbye!"],["variations","Variations","5 Sekretärin: Danke für den Anruf. Ich sage der Lehrerin Bescheid. :: Thanks for the call. I'll let the teacher know."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Call before school starts. Many schools also accept an e-mail or a message in the school app. Auf Wiederhören is the goodbye of the phone."]]},{"u":"anrufen.html","t":"anrufen","s":"to phone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Schule hat gerade angerufen. :: The school just called. Bitte rufen Sie wieder an. :: Please call again."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich anrufe die Schule. :: Ich rufe die Schule an."]]},{"u":"antwort-trainer-training-bei-hitze.html","t":"Antwort des Trainers: Training bei Hitze","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo, ist ok, für alle zur Info: Hello, that's OK. For everyone's information: Wir werden nur lockere Übungen machen und ein paar Standards, keine großartigen anstrengenden Dinge. We will only do light exercises and a few set pieces, nothing very strenuous. Gruß Regards"],["notes","Notes","Standards in football are set pieces: free kicks, corners, throw-ins. locker here means light, relaxed. keine großartigen ... Dinge is colloquial for \"nothing big\". für alle zur Info tells you the coach answers one parent but writes for the whole group."]]},{"u":"anziehen.html","t":"anziehen","s":"to put on / to dress","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zieh dich bitte an! :: Please get dressed! Ich ziehe die Jacke an. :: I put on the jacket."],["notes","Notes","sich anziehen : to get dressed. Zieh dich an! to a child."]]},{"u":"arbeit.html","t":"Arbeit","s":"work / job","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach der Arbeit hole ich die Kinder ab. :: After work I pick up the children."]]},{"u":"arbeiten.html","t":"arbeiten","s":"to work","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. :: I have to work until six. Können Sie morgen von zu Hause arbeiten? :: Can you work from home tomorrow?"]]},{"u":"aua.html","t":"aua","s":"ouch","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Aua! Mein Knie tut weh. :: Ouch! My knee hurts."]]},{"u":"auch.html","t":"auch","s":"also / too","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Would you like a coffee too? Ich dich auch. :: Me too."]]},{"u":"auf-der-tribuene.html","t":"Auf der Tribüne","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Vater: Hallo! Spielt deine Tochter heute auch? :: Hi! Is your daughter playing today too? ich: Ja, sie ist die Nummer sieben, im Tor. :: Yes, she's number seven, in goal. Vater: Toll! Wie steht es? :: Great! What's the score? ich: Zwölf zu zehn für uns. Aber die andere Mannschaft ist sehr stark. :: Twelve to ten for us. But the other team is very strong. Vater: Oh, ein Foul! Das war doch kein Siebenmeter! :: Oh, a foul! That was no penalty! ich: Doch, der Schiedsrichter hat recht. :: Yes it was, the referee is right. Vater: Na ja. Noch fünf Minuten. Hoffentlich gewinnen wir! :: Oh well. Five more minutes. Hopefully we'll win!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Zehn zu zehn. Es ist sehr spannend! :: Ten all. It's very exciting!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Siebenmeter is the penalty throw in handball. Doch says yes against a negative sentence."]]},{"u":"auf-eigene-gefahr.html","t":"auf eigene Gefahr","s":"at your own risk","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sie betreten den Wald auf eigene Gefahr. :: You enter the forest at your own risk. Unbefugtes Parken auf eigene Gefahr! :: Parking without permission at your own risk! Benutzung auf eigene Gefahr. :: Use at your own risk."],["usage","Usage","On signs and notices: the owner says they are not responsible if something happens to you or your car. Always eigene without article."]]},{"u":"auf-wiederhoeren.html","t":"Auf Wiederhören!","s":"Goodbye! (on the phone)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Danke, auf Wiederhören! :: Thank you, goodbye! Auf Wiedersehen! :: Goodbye! (face to face)"],["usage","Usage","On the phone you hear each other again, so Wiederhören ."]]},{"u":"auf.html","t":"auf","s":"on / onto","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist auf unserem Platz. :: The match is on our pitch."]]},{"u":"aufraeumen.html","t":"aufräumen","s":"to tidy up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Räum bitte dein Zimmer auf! :: Please tidy up your room!"]]},{"u":"aufstehen.html","t":"aufstehen","s":"to get up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir stehen um halb sieben auf. :: We get up at half past six."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich aufstehe um sechs. :: Ich stehe um sechs auf."]]},{"u":"aus.html","t":"aus","s":"from / out of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag spielen wir gegen die Mannschaft aus der Nachbarstadt. :: On Saturday we play against the team from the neighbouring town."],["notes","Notes","aus for where someone comes from: Ich komme aus Spanien."]]},{"u":"ausfallen.html","t":"ausfallen","s":"to be cancelled","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wegen Regen fällt das Training heute leider aus. :: Because of rain, training is cancelled today."]]},{"u":"ausflug.html","t":"Ausflug","s":"trip / outing","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Dezember machen wir einen Ausflug ins Museum. :: In December we are going on a trip to the museum."]]},{"u":"ausgenommen.html","t":"ausgenommen","s":"except","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Halteverbot gilt für alle, ausgenommen Linienbusse. :: The no-stopping rule applies to everyone except scheduled buses. Die Durchfahrt ist verboten, Anlieger ausgenommen. :: No through traffic, residents excepted."],["notes","Notes","Very common on extra plates under traffic signs. It can come before or after the noun. Anlieger frei says the same thing for residents."]]},{"u":"ausrichten.html","t":"ausrichten","s":"to host, to organise (an event)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am JSG-Tag richten alle teilnehmenden Mannschaften ein Spiel aus. :: On JSG day all participating teams host a match. Kannst du dem Trainer etwas ausrichten? :: Can you pass a message on to the coach?"],["notes","Notes","Two meanings: to host an event ( ein Turnier ausrichten ), and to pass on a message ( jemandem etwas ausrichten , + Dativ for the person)."]]},{"u":"bald.html","t":"bald","s":"soon","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bis bald! :: See you soon!"]]},{"u":"ball.html","t":"Ball","s":"ball","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe drei Bälle gehalten. :: I saved three balls."]]},{"u":"beantragen.html","t":"beantragen","s":"to apply for","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Eine der Vertragsparteien wird die Förderung innerhalb von 14 Tagen nach Vertragsschluss beantragen. :: One of the parties to the contract will apply for the subsidy within 14 days of signing. Wir haben die Förderung bei der KfW beantragt. :: We have applied for the subsidy from the KfW. Ich beantrage einen Grundbuchauszug. :: I am applying for an extract from the land register."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wir haben für die Förderung beantragt. :: Wir haben die Förderung beantragt. Ich antrage die Förderung. :: Ich beantrage die Förderung."],["notes","Notes","be- is never separated: ich beantrage , beantragt . The thing you apply for is in the accusative, without für . The same with a noun: einen Antrag stellen , einen Antrag auf Förderung stellen ."]]},{"u":"beeil-dich.html","t":"Beeil dich!","s":"Hurry up!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Beeilt euch, der Bus kommt! :: Hurry up, the bus is coming! (to several) Wir müssen uns beeilen. :: We have to hurry."],["usage","Usage","To a child in the morning. sich beeilen is reflexive."]]},{"u":"bei-bedarf.html","t":"bei Bedarf","s":"if needed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Der Zug hält dort nur bei Bedarf. :: The train only stops there on request. Bei Bedarf rufen Sie mich bitte an. :: Call me if needed."],["usage","Usage","In a train, Halt bei Bedarf means the train only stops when someone presses the stop button ( Haltewunsch ) or waits on the platform. In letters and offices it means \"if you need it\"."]]},{"u":"bei.html","t":"bei","s":"at / with","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Paketbote hat es bei mir abgegeben. :: The delivery man left it with me."],["notes","Notes","beim Arzt : at the doctor's. bei mir : at my place."]]},{"u":"bescheid-geben.html","t":"Bescheid geben","s":"to let someone know","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ich wollte kurz Bescheid geben, dass er heute nicht kommt. :: I just wanted to let you know that he isn't coming today. Gib mir bitte Bescheid, wenn das Training ausfällt. :: Please let me know if training is cancelled. Geben Sie uns bitte bis Freitag Bescheid. :: Please let us know by Friday. (formal)"],["usage","Usage","The usual way to tell the coach that your child is missing. The person gets the dative: mir, dir, Ihnen, euch . Bescheid sagen means the same."]]},{"u":"bescheid-sagen.html","t":"Bescheid sagen","s":"to let someone know","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sag mir Bescheid! :: Let me know! Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen. :: Thank you for letting me know. Wer keine Zeit hat, sagt mir bitte bis Montag Bescheid. :: Whoever has no time, please let me know by Monday."],["usage","Usage","When you promise to tell someone later, or thank someone for telling you. The person is in the Dativ: mir , dir , Ihnen ."]]},{"u":"besonders.html","t":"besonders","s":"especially / particularly","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel war besonders spannend. :: The match was particularly exciting."],["notes","Notes","Before a noun the adjective is besondere : Heute ist ein besonderer Tag."]]},{"u":"besprechung-verschoben.html","t":"Besprechung verschoben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo zusammen, Hello everyone, die Besprechung am Montag ist leider verschoben. Monday's meeting has unfortunately been postponed. Wir treffen uns jetzt am Dienstag um 14 Uhr im Raum 3. We now meet on Tuesday at 2 pm in room 3. Bitte bringt eure Zahlen vom Oktober mit. Please bring your figures from October. Wer keine Zeit hat, sagt mir bitte bis Montag Bescheid. Whoever has no time, please let me know by Monday. Viele Grüße Best regards Die Teamleiterin The team leader"],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. verschoben is the participle of verschieben : to postpone. In Germany, times at work are written with the 24-hour clock: 14 Uhr is 2 pm."]]},{"u":"besprechung.html","t":"Besprechung","s":"meeting","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Um zehn habe ich eine Besprechung. :: At ten I have a meeting."]]},{"u":"besuchen.html","t":"besuchen","s":"to visit","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Wochenende besuchen wir die Großeltern. :: At the weekend we visit the grandparents."],["notes","Notes","Verbs with be- have no ge- in the Perfekt: besucht ."]]},{"u":"betreten.html","t":"betreten","s":"to enter","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie betreten den Wald auf eigene Gefahr. :: You enter the forest at your own risk. Unbefugtes Betreten ist verboten. :: Entry without permission is forbidden."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich betrete in den Wald. :: Ich betrete den Wald."],["notes","Notes","betreten takes a direct object, without in . It sounds formal: in everyday speech you say in den Wald gehen . On signs: Betreten verboten , Rasen nicht betreten ."]]},{"u":"bett.html","t":"Bett","s":"bed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist acht Uhr. Zeit fürs Bett! :: It is eight o'clock. Time for bed!"]]},{"u":"billig.html","t":"billig","s":"cheap","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Supermarkt ist der Kaffee billiger. :: Coffee is cheaper in the supermarket."],["notes","Notes","günstig sounds more positive: good value."]]},{"u":"bis-morgen.html","t":"Bis morgen!","s":"See you tomorrow!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Bis später! :: See you later! Bis bald! :: See you soon! Bis Samstag! :: See you on Saturday!"],["usage","Usage","bis plus a time says when you will see each other again."]]},{"u":"bis.html","t":"bis","s":"until / by","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie den Zettel bis Dienstag zurück. :: Please return the slip by Tuesday. Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. :: I have to work until six."],["notes","Notes","Usually without an article: bis Montag , bis acht Uhr . With an article it needs zu : bis zum Ende ."]]},{"u":"bitte.html","t":"bitte","s":"please / you're welcome","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: Five more minutes, please! Ja, bitte. Was gibt's? :: Yes, please. What is it?"],["notes","Notes","Bitte? alone means Pardon? . Bitte! also answers Danke!"]]},{"u":"bleiben.html","t":"bleiben","s":"to stay","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie bleibt heute zu Hause. :: She is staying at home today."]]},{"u":"bleibt-sportlich.html","t":"Bleibt sportlich!","s":"stay sporty (sports-club sign-off)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Bis dahin, bleibt sportlich! :: Until then, stay sporty! Mit sportlichen Grüßen :: With sporting regards"],["usage","Usage","A friendly closing in sports clubs, like Viele Grüße . Mit sportlichen Grüßen is the written, slightly more formal version."]]},{"u":"brauchen.html","t":"brauchen","s":"to need","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich brauche heute einen Termin. :: I need an appointment today. Wir brauchen noch zwei Autos. :: We still need two cars."]]},{"u":"brotdose.html","t":"Brotdose","s":"lunch box","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du deine Brotdose? :: Do you have your lunch box?"]]},{"u":"bruder.html","t":"Bruder","s":"brother","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Bruder wohnt in Spanien. :: My brother lives in Spain."]]},{"u":"buero.html","t":"Büro","s":"office","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgen arbeite ich nicht im Büro, sondern von zu Hause. :: Tomorrow I am not working in the office but from home."]]},{"u":"chat-der-fussballeltern.html","t":"Chat der Fußballeltern","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Trainer: Hallo zusammen! Wegen Regen fällt das Training heute leider aus. Coach: Hello everyone! Because of the rain, training is cancelled today. Trainer: Am Samstag spielen wir um zehn Uhr in der Nachbarstadt. Treffpunkt ist um neun Uhr am Vereinsheim. Coach: On Saturday we play at ten o'clock in the neighbouring town. The meeting point is at nine o'clock at the clubhouse. Trainer: Wer kann fahren? Wir brauchen noch zwei Autos. Coach: Who can drive? We still need two cars. Mutter: Ich kann fahren und habe drei Plätze frei. Mother: I can drive and have three free seats. Vater: Mein Sohn ist krank und kann leider nicht mitspielen. Father: My son is ill and unfortunately cannot play. Trainer: Danke euch! Gute Besserung an deinen Sohn. Coach: Thank you all! Get well soon to your son."],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. fällt aus comes from ausfallen , a separable verb: to be cancelled. To answer, one short line is enough: Ich kann auch fahren. or Mein Sohn kommt."]]},{"u":"chefin.html","t":"Chefin","s":"boss (woman)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich frage die Chefin, ob ich früher gehen kann. :: I ask the boss whether I can leave early."],["notes","Notes","A man is der Chef , plural die Chefs ."]]},{"u":"da.html","t":"da","s":"there / then","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er soll um halb zehn da sein. :: He should be there at half past nine. Am Vormittag nicht, da hat mein Sohn ein Spiel. :: Not in the morning, my son has a match then."],["notes","Notes","da sein : to be there, to be present."]]},{"u":"danach.html","t":"danach","s":"afterwards","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Danach essen wir zusammen Pizza. :: Afterwards we eat pizza together."]]},{"u":"danke.html","t":"danke","s":"thank you / thanks","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Danke, das ist nett. :: Thanks, that's kind. Vielen Dank! :: Thank you very much!"],["notes","Notes","The answer is Bitte! or Gern geschehen!"]]},{"u":"dann.html","t":"dann","s":"then","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play."]]},{"u":"darf-ich-kurz-stoeren.html","t":"Darf ich kurz stören?","s":"May I interrupt for a moment?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Entschuldigung, darf ich kurz stören? :: Excuse me, may I interrupt for a moment? Haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Do you have a moment?"],["usage","Usage","Before you ask a boss or a teacher something, at the door of their office."]]},{"u":"das-tut-mir-leid.html","t":"Das tut mir leid.","s":"I'm sorry.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Oh, das tut mir leid! :: Oh, I'm sorry! Es tut mir leid, ich bin zu spät. :: I'm sorry, I'm late."],["usage","Usage","When something bad happened, or to apologise. For a small thing, Entschuldigung! is enough."]]},{"u":"das.html","t":"das","s":"the (neuter)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Training fällt aus. :: Training is cancelled."],["notes","Notes","Neuter: das , das , dem . das also means that : Das ist nett."]]},{"u":"dass.html","t":"dass","s":"that","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen. :: Thank you for letting me know."]]},{"u":"dativ.html","t":"Dativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The Dativ is the case of the person who receives or is helped, and the case after mit, bei, nach, von, zu, seit, aus . masculine feminine neuter plural Nominativ der / ein die / eine das / ein die Dativ dem / einem der / einer dem / einem den (+ n) Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn. Wir gehen zum Arzt. Ich helfe dir . Ich gebe den Kinder n einen Apfel. Short forms: zum = zu dem , zur = zu der , beim = bei dem , vom = von dem ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Nach mit, bei, nach, von, zu, seit, aus steht der Dativ: mit dem Ball, mit der Mannschaft . Verben wie helfen haben den Dativ: Ich helfe dir ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich spiele mit mein Sohn. :: Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn. Wir fahren zu die Halle. :: Wir fahren zur Halle."]]},{"u":"dein.html","t":"dein","s":"your (informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du deine Brotdose? :: Do you have your lunch box?"],["notes","Notes","Endings like ein ."]]},{"u":"denn.html","t":"denn","s":"because","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich komme nicht, denn ich muss arbeiten. :: I am not coming because I have to work."],["notes","Notes","denn and weil both mean because . After denn the verb stays in position 2."]]},{"u":"der-die-das.html","t":"Der, die, das","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Every German noun has a gender: masculine der , feminine die or neuter das . In the plural all nouns take die . Learn each noun with its article: der Ball, die Mannschaft, das Tor . Some endings help: -ung , -heit , -keit and -in are always die ( die Wohnung , die Lehrerin ); -chen is always das ( das Mädchen ). The site colours nouns by gender: blue der , red die , green das , orange plural."],["simple-german","Simple German","Jedes Nomen hat einen Artikel: der , die oder das . Im Plural ist der Artikel immer die . Lerne das Nomen immer mit Artikel."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","die Training :: das Training der Wohnung :: die Wohnung"]]},{"u":"der.html","t":"der","s":"the (masculine)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Trainer schreibt alles in den Chat. :: The coach writes everything in the chat."],["notes","Notes","Masculine: der (Nominativ), den (Akkusativ), dem (Dativ). der is also the Dativ of die : mit der Mannschaft ."]]},{"u":"deshalb.html","t":"deshalb","s":"that is why","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist krank, deshalb bleibt er zu Hause. :: My son is ill, that is why he is staying at home."]]},{"u":"die-neue-nachbarin.html","t":"Die neue Nachbarin","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Nachbarin: Guten Tag! Ich bin die neue Nachbarin. Ich wohne im zweiten Stock. :: Hello! I'm the new neighbour. I live on the second floor. ich: Guten Tag und herzlich willkommen! Wir wohnen hier im Erdgeschoss. :: Hello and welcome! We live here on the ground floor. Nachbarin: Freut mich. Wohnen Sie schon lange hier? :: Nice to meet you. Have you lived here long? ich: Seit drei Jahren. Das Haus ist sehr ruhig. :: For three years. The house is very quiet. Nachbarin: Wann kommt hier die Müllabfuhr? :: When does the rubbish collection come here? ich: Am Mittwoch. Die Mülltonnen stehen im Hof. :: On Wednesday. The bins are in the yard. Nachbarin: Danke schön! Einen schönen Tag noch. :: Thank you! Have a nice day. ich: Danke, gleichfalls! :: Thanks, you too!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Seit einem Jahr. Die Nachbarn sind sehr nett. :: For a year. The neighbours are very nice."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. seit plus the present tense: Wir wohnen seit drei Jahren hier means we have lived here for three years . The German Erdgeschoss is the ground floor; der erste Stock is the floor above it."]]},{"u":"die.html","t":"die","s":"the (feminine / plural)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Lehrerin hat angerufen. :: The teacher called. Die Kinder spielen im Garten. :: The children are playing in the garden."],["notes","Notes","Feminine and all plurals. The Dativ plural is den and the noun gets -n : mit den Kindern ."]]},{"u":"dieser.html","t":"dieser","s":"this","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Diese Woche fährt die Oma. :: This week grandma is driving. Dieses Spiel war spannend. :: This match was exciting."],["notes","Notes","Endings like der, die, das : dieser, diese, dieses ."]]},{"u":"doch.html","t":"doch","s":"yes (contradicting) / just","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das war doch kein Siebenmeter! Doch, der Schiedsrichter hat recht. :: That was no penalty! Yes it was, the referee is right."],["notes","Notes","Doch answers yes to a negative question or sentence. In Frag doch mal! it makes a suggestion softer."]]},{"u":"dort.html","t":"dort","s":"there","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Café am Marktplatz? Dort treffen wir uns. :: The café on the market square? We'll meet there."]]},{"u":"draussen.html","t":"draußen","s":"outside","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Kinder spielen draußen im Garten. :: The children are playing outside in the garden."]]},{"u":"drei.html","t":"drei","s":"three","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe drei Plätze frei. :: I have three free seats."]]},{"u":"dritte.html","t":"dritte","s":"third","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am dritten Tag ist er wieder gesund. :: On the third day he is healthy again."],["notes","Notes","Irregular, like erste : not dreite ."]]},{"u":"du.html","t":"du","s":"you (informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich rufe dich morgen an. :: I will call you tomorrow. Ich helfe dir gern. :: I am happy to help you."],["notes","Notes","du for children, family, friends, and often parents at school and in the sports club."]]},{"u":"duerfen.html","t":"dürfen","s":"may / to be allowed to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: May I watch TV for ten more minutes?"],["notes","Notes","nicht dürfen means must not : Du darfst hier nicht spielen ."]]},{"u":"durch.html","t":"durch","s":"through","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen durch den Park zur Schule. :: We walk through the park to school."]]},{"u":"eigentlich.html","t":"eigentlich","s":"actually","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was machst du eigentlich am Wochenende? :: So what are you doing at the weekend? Eigentlich habe ich keine Zeit, aber ich komme. :: Actually I have no time, but I'll come."],["notes","Notes","In a question it makes it softer and more personal."]]},{"u":"ein-paket-fuer-die-nachbarn.html","t":"Ein Paket für die Nachbarn","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Guten Abend! Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. Der Paketbote hat es heute Morgen bei mir abgegeben. :: Good evening! I have a parcel for you. The delivery man left it with me this morning. Nachbar: Oh, vielen Dank! Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: Oh, thank you very much! That's very kind of you. ich: Gern geschehen. :: You're welcome. Nachbar: Übrigens, am Samstag feiern wir den Geburtstag von unserem Sohn. Es wird vielleicht ein bisschen laut. :: By the way, on Saturday we are celebrating our son's birthday. It might get a bit loud. ich: Kein Problem. Bis wann geht die Party? :: No problem. Until when does the party go on? Nachbar: Bis zehn Uhr, versprochen! :: Until ten o'clock, I promise! ich: Dann viel Spaß beim Feiern! :: Then have fun celebrating!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Accepting a parcel for a neighbour is normal in Germany. The delivery service leaves a card in the neighbour's letter box."]]},{"u":"ein-tor-schiessen.html","t":"ein Tor schießen","s":"to score a goal","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Er hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: He scored two goals. Wer hat das Tor geschossen? :: Who scored the goal?"],["usage","Usage","In football. In handball people say ein Tor werfen : to throw a goal."]]},{"u":"ein.html","t":"ein","s":"a / an","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. :: I have a parcel for you."],["notes","Notes","ein for der and das words, eine for die words. Akkusativ masculine: einen Termin ."]]},{"u":"einen-termin-vereinbaren.html","t":"einen Termin vereinbaren","s":"to make an appointment","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ich möchte einen Termin vereinbaren. :: I would like to make an appointment. Ich brauche einen Termin beim Kinderarzt. :: I need an appointment with the paediatrician."],["usage","Usage","On the phone with a practice, the school or an office."]]},{"u":"einfach.html","t":"einfach","s":"simple / easy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Aufgabe ist ganz einfach. :: The task is very easy. Komm doch einfach mit! :: Just come along!"],["notes","Notes","As a particle, einfach means just : Ruf einfach an!"]]},{"u":"einkaufen.html","t":"einkaufen","s":"to go shopping","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach der Arbeit kaufe ich schnell ein. :: After work I do some quick shopping."]]},{"u":"einladen.html","t":"einladen","s":"to invite","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich lade dich und deine Familie herzlich ein! :: I warmly invite you and your family!"]]},{"u":"einladung-zum-geburtstag.html","t":"Einladung zum Geburtstag","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo! Wie geht es dir? Wir haben uns so lange nicht gesehen. Hi! How are you? We haven't seen each other for so long. Am Freitag mache ich eine kleine Party, weil ich Geburtstag habe. On Friday I'm having a small party because it's my birthday. Ich lade dich und deine Familie herzlich ein! I warmly invite you and your family! Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. Die Kinder können im Garten spielen. We start at six o'clock. The children can play in the garden. Kannst du mir bis Mittwoch Bescheid sagen, ob ihr kommt? Can you let me know by Wednesday whether you are coming? Liebe Grüße! Love!"],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. The message asks for an answer by Wednesday. A short reply: Danke für die Einladung! Wir kommen gern."]]},{"u":"eins.html","t":"eins","s":"one","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir kommen so gegen eins. :: We'll come around one."],["notes","Notes","Counting and alone: eins . Before a noun it is the article ein, eine . With Uhr : ein Uhr ."]]},{"u":"elf.html","t":"elf","s":"eleven","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommen Sie bitte um elf Uhr. :: Please come at eleven o'clock."]]},{"u":"eltern.html","t":"Eltern","s":"parents","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Eltern treffen sich am Donnerstag in der Schule. :: The parents meet at school on Thursday."],["notes","Notes","Only plural: die Eltern . One parent is der Elternteil , but people usually say Mutter or Vater ."]]},{"u":"elternabend.html","t":"Elternabend","s":"parents' evening","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommst du am Donnerstag zum Elternabend? :: Are you coming to the parents' evening on Thursday?"]]},{"u":"entschuldigung.html","t":"Entschuldigung","s":"excuse note / apology","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Muss ich eine Entschuldigung schreiben? :: Do I have to write an excuse note?"],["notes","Notes","Alone, Entschuldigung! means Excuse me! or Sorry! . At school, eine Entschuldigung is the note that explains why a child was absent."]]},{"u":"er.html","t":"er","s":"he / it","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie ihm einen kurzen Zettel mit. :: Please give him a short note to take. Ich hole ihn um vier ab. :: I will pick him up at four."],["notes","Notes","er also stands for a masculine thing: der Ball, er ist rot ."]]},{"u":"erkaeltung.html","t":"Erkältung","s":"cold","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist nur eine Erkältung. :: It is only a cold."]]},{"u":"erste.html","t":"erste","s":"first","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter geht in die erste Klasse. :: My daughter is in first grade. Am ersten Tag war sie sehr müde. :: On the first day she was very tired."],["notes","Notes","Ordinals: erste, zweite, dritte, vierte , then -te up to 19 and -ste from 20: zwanzigste ."]]},{"u":"es.html","t":"es","s":"it","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wo ist die Brotdose? Ich finde sie nicht. :: Where is the lunch box? I can't find it. Es regnet. Es ist schon spät. :: It's raining. It's already late."],["notes","Notes","es is for das words. For der and die words, it is er and sie . es also starts sentences about weather and time."]]},{"u":"essen.html","t":"essen","s":"to eat","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Können wir Pizza essen? :: Can we eat pizza?"]]},{"u":"etwas.html","t":"etwas","s":"something","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Müssen die Kinder etwas mitbringen? :: Do the children have to bring anything?"],["notes","Notes","Short form in speech: was . etwas before a noun means some : etwas Wasser ."]]},{"u":"euer.html","t":"euer","s":"your (plural informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte bringt eure Zahlen vom Oktober mit. :: Please bring your figures from October."],["notes","Notes","The e drops before an ending: eure , euren ."]]},{"u":"fahren.html","t":"fahren","s":"to drive / to go (by vehicle)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Fährst du am Dienstag zum Training? :: Are you driving to training on Tuesday? Wir sind mit dem Bus gefahren. :: We went by bus."],["notes","Notes","sein when you go somewhere; haben when you drive someone or something: Ich habe die Kinder gefahren ."]]},{"u":"fahrgemeinschaft.html","t":"Fahrgemeinschaft","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Mutter: Hallo! Fährst du am Dienstag zum Training? :: Hi! Are you driving to training on Tuesday? ich: Ja, warum? :: Yes, why? Mutter: Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. Kannst du meine Tochter mitnehmen? :: I have to work until six. Can you take my daughter along? ich: Na klar, kein Problem. Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: Of course, no problem. I'll pick her up at quarter past four. Mutter: Danke! Und ich fahre dafür am Donnerstag. :: Thanks! And I'll drive on Thursday in return. ich: Abgemacht! :: Deal!"],["variations","Variations","2 ich: Nein, diese Woche kann ich leider nicht. Frag doch mal im Chat. :: No, sadly I can't this week. Why don't you ask in the chat."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. A Fahrgemeinschaft is a lift share: parents take turns driving the children."]]},{"u":"falsch.html","t":"falsch","s":"wrong","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Diese Aufgabe ist falsch. Rechne noch einmal! :: This task is wrong. Do the sum again!"]]},{"u":"familie.html","t":"Familie","s":"family","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Familie wohnt seit drei Jahren in Deutschland. :: My family has lived in Germany for three years. Am Sonntag frühstücken wir als Familie zusammen. :: On Sunday we have breakfast together as a family."]]},{"u":"feierabend-machen.html","t":"Feierabend machen","s":"to finish work for the day","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ich mache heute um vier Feierabend. :: I'm finishing work at four today. Schönen Feierabend! :: Enjoy your evening! (after work)"],["usage","Usage","Schönen Feierabend! is what colleagues say when someone goes home."]]},{"u":"feierabend.html","t":"Feierabend","s":"end of the working day","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Um fünf habe ich Feierabend. :: I finish work at five."]]},{"u":"feiern.html","t":"feiern","s":"to celebrate","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag feiern wir den Geburtstag von unserem Sohn. :: On Saturday we are celebrating our son's birthday."]]},{"u":"fernsehen.html","t":"fernsehen","s":"to watch TV","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: May I watch TV for ten more minutes?"]]},{"u":"fertig.html","t":"fertig","s":"ready / finished","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bist du fertig? Wir müssen los! :: Are you ready? We have to go! Ich mache die Präsentation morgen fertig. :: I'll finish the presentation tomorrow."],["notes","Notes","fertig sein : to be ready or finished. fertig machen : to finish something."]]},{"u":"feuerwehrzufahrt.html","t":"Feuerwehrzufahrt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Feuerwehrzufahrt Zuschauereingang Gas"],["meaning","Meaning","The round white sign with a red ring means: no vehicles of any kind ( Verbot für Fahrzeuge aller Art ). The sign below says why: this is the access road for the fire brigade ( Feuerwehrzufahrt ). It must always stay clear, so never park or stop here. The small yellow sign marks a gas valve under the ground. On the wall, an arrow shows the way to the spectators' entrance ( Zuschauereingang )."]]},{"u":"fieber.html","t":"Fieber","s":"fever / temperature","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er hat seit gestern Fieber und Husten. :: He has had a fever and a cough since yesterday."]]},{"u":"foerderung.html","t":"Förderung","s":"subsidy, grant","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die angegebene Förderung ist voraussichtlich und abhängig von Bewilligung sowie Auszahlung durch die KfW. :: The subsidy stated is an estimate and depends on approval and payment by the KfW. Die Förderung erhalten Sie separat direkt von der KfW. :: You receive the subsidy separately, directly from the KfW. Unsere Förderung ist bewilligt. :: Our subsidy has been approved."],["notes","Notes","A subsidy is bewilligt (approved) or abgelehnt (refused). The letter that approves it is the Zusage or Zusageschreiben ."]]},{"u":"frage-15-minuten-vor-dem-training.html","t":"Frage: 15 Minuten vor dem Training da sein?","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Vater: Hallo. Ich habe gehört das man 15min vor Trainings Beginn da sein soll. Stimmt das? :: Hello. I heard that you should be there 15 minutes before training starts. Is that true? Trainer: Hallo, wenn es sich einrichten lässt, ja. Wenn wir pünktlich starten möchten, ist das leider notwendig. Gruß, Herr M. :: Hello, if it can be arranged, yes. If we want to start on time, it is unfortunately necessary. Regards, Mr M. Vater: Ok. Kein Problem, wollte nur sichergehen. :: OK. No problem, I just wanted to make sure."],["variations","Variations","1 Vater: Hallo. Ich habe gehört, dass man 15 Minuten vor Trainingsbeginn da sein soll. Stimmt das? :: Hello. I heard that you should be there 15 minutes before training starts. Is that true?"],["notes","Notes","A real chat between another parent and the coach, kept word for word. The variation shows the correct spelling: dass (conjunction) with a comma, Trainingsbeginn as one word. wenn es sich einrichten lässt : if it can be arranged. Polite and useful. sichergehen : to make sure. Ich wollte nur sichergehen."]]},{"u":"frei.html","t":"frei","s":"free / available","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe drei Plätze frei. :: I have three free seats. Am Samstag habe ich frei. :: I'm off on Saturday."],["notes","Notes","frei can also mean free of charge , but usually that is kostenlos ."]]},{"u":"freuen.html","t":"freuen","s":"to be happy / to look forward","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Kinder freuen sich. :: Our children will be happy. Ich freue mich auf das Wochenende. :: I am looking forward to the weekend."],["notes","Notes","sich freuen auf : to look forward to. sich freuen über : to be happy about. Das freut mich! I'm glad!"]]},{"u":"freund.html","t":"Freund","s":"friend / boyfriend","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Sonntag grillen wir mit Freunden im Garten. :: On Sunday we are having a barbecue with friends in the garden."],["notes","Notes","mein Freund often means my boyfriend . For a friend people say ein Freund von mir ."]]},{"u":"freundin.html","t":"Freundin","s":"friend (woman) / girlfriend","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Freundin hat am Freitag Geburtstag. :: My friend has her birthday on Friday."]]},{"u":"freundlich.html","t":"freundlich","s":"friendly","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die neue Nachbarin ist sehr freundlich. :: The new neighbour is very friendly."]]},{"u":"freut-mich.html","t":"Freut mich!","s":"Nice to meet you!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Freut mich, Sie kennenzulernen. :: Nice to meet you. (Sie) Das freut mich! :: I'm glad!"],["usage","Usage","When someone tells you their name for the first time."]]},{"u":"frueh.html","t":"früh","s":"early","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kann ich heute früher gehen? :: Can I leave earlier today?"]]},{"u":"frueher-gehen.html","t":"Früher gehen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, darf ich kurz stören? :: Excuse me, may I interrupt for a moment? Chefin: Ja, bitte. Was gibt's? :: Yes, please. What is it? ich: Meine Tochter ist krank. Die Schule hat gerade angerufen. Kann ich heute früher gehen? :: My daughter is ill. The school just called. Can I leave early today? Chefin: Natürlich, das ist kein Problem. Gute Besserung für Ihre Tochter! :: Of course, that's no problem. Get well soon to your daughter! ich: Danke. Ich mache die Präsentation morgen fertig. :: Thanks. I'll finish the presentation tomorrow. Chefin: Gut. Können Sie morgen von zu Hause arbeiten? :: Good. Can you work from home tomorrow? ich: Ja, das geht. Ich schreibe Ihnen eine E-Mail. :: Yes, that works. I'll write you an email."],["variations","Variations","4 Chefin: Hm, heute ist es schwierig. Können Sie bis drei Uhr bleiben? :: Hm, today is difficult. Can you stay until three?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. In Germany parents may stay at home with an ill child ( Kinderkrankentage ); the paediatrician gives a certificate for the employer."]]},{"u":"fruehstueck.html","t":"Frühstück","s":"breakfast","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast?"]]},{"u":"fruehstuecken.html","t":"frühstücken","s":"to have breakfast","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Komm frühstücken! :: Come and have breakfast!"]]},{"u":"fuenf.html","t":"fünf","s":"five","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: Five more minutes, please!"]]},{"u":"fuer.html","t":"für","s":"for","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. :: I have a parcel for you."]]},{"u":"fussball.html","t":"Fußball","s":"football","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn spielt seit zwei Jahren Fußball. :: My son has been playing football for two years."],["notes","Notes","Fußball spielen is the sport, without article. Der Fußball is also the ball itself."]]},{"u":"gap-faellt-das-training-aus.html","t":"Fällt das Training aus?","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","Is training cancelled today because of the rain?"],["in-german","In German","Fällt das Training heute wegen des Regens aus?"]]},{"u":"gap-heute-holt-die-oma-ab.html","t":"Heute holt die Oma ab","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","Today grandma is picking up our daughter, not me."],["in-german","In German","Heute holt die Oma unsere Tochter ab, nicht ich."]]},{"u":"gap-paket-annehmen.html","t":"Paket annehmen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","Could you accept a parcel for me tomorrow? I'm at work all day."],["in-german","In German","Könnten Sie morgen ein Paket für mich annehmen? Ich bin den ganzen Tag bei der Arbeit."]]},{"u":"gap-sporttasche-vergessen.html","t":"Sporttasche vergessen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","My son forgot his sports bag at home. Can I bring it at five?"],["in-german","In German","Mein Sohn hat seine Sporttasche zu Hause vergessen. Kann ich sie um fünf bringen?"]]},{"u":"geben.html","t":"geben","s":"to give","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast? Bei Fieber geben Sie ihm den Saft. :: If he has a fever, give him the syrup."],["notes","Notes","es gibt plus Akkusativ means there is or there are ."]]},{"u":"geburtstag.html","t":"Geburtstag","s":"birthday","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Freitag mache ich eine kleine Party, weil ich Geburtstag habe. :: On Friday I am having a small party because it is my birthday."]]},{"u":"gefahr.html","t":"Gefahr","s":"danger","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Damit steigt die Gefahr durch herabfallende Äste und umfallende Bäume. :: So the danger from falling branches and falling trees rises. Erkennen Sie die Gefahr? :: Do you recognise the danger?"],["notes","Notes","Do not mix up die Gefahren (the dangers) with gefahren (participle of fahren ): Gefahren durch klimakranke Bäume and Hier wird schnell gefahren sound almost the same."]]},{"u":"gefahren-durch-klimakranke-baeume.html","t":"Gefahren durch klimakranke Bäume","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Gefahren durch klimakranke Bäume Erkennen Sie die Gefahr? Liebe Waldgäste, Dürrephasen nehmen durch die Klimakrise zu und schädigen viele Bäume. Damit steigt die Gefahr durch herabfallende Äste und umfallende Bäume. Sie betreten den Wald auf eigene Gefahr. Daher: Seien Sie beim Waldbesuch besonders aufmerksam und schauen Sie nach oben in die Baumkronen. Achten Sie auf absterbende oder lose Baumteile und meiden Sie deren Nähe. Insbesondere bei Wind können sehr gefährliche Situationen entstehen. Im Notfall: 112. Nach Möglichkeit mit Nennung eines Rettungspunktes."],["meaning","Meaning","Dangers from trees made sick by the climate. Do you recognise the danger? Dear forest visitors, dry periods are increasing because of the climate crisis and damage many trees. So the danger from falling branches and falling trees rises. You enter the forest at your own risk. Therefore: be especially careful when you visit the forest and look up into the treetops. Watch out for dying or loose parts of trees and keep away from them. Above all when it is windy, very dangerous situations can arise. In an emergency call 112, and if possible name a rescue point ( Rettungspunkt ): the green signs with a number along forest roads, where an ambulance can find you."]]},{"u":"gegen.html","t":"gegen","s":"against","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag spielen wir gegen die Mannschaft aus der Nachbarstadt. :: On Saturday we play against the team from the neighbouring town."],["notes","Notes","gegen eins also means around one o'clock ."]]},{"u":"gegenueber.html","t":"gegenüber","s":"opposite","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Café ist gegenüber der Schule. :: The café is opposite the school."]]},{"u":"gehen.html","t":"gehen","s":"to go / to walk","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: We are going to the paediatrician today. Ich bin gestern zum Training gegangen. :: I went to training yesterday."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe nach Hause gegangen. :: Ich bin nach Hause gegangen."],["notes","Notes","Wie geht's? How are you? Das geht. That works."]]},{"u":"gerade.html","t":"gerade","s":"just / right now","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Schule hat gerade angerufen. :: The school just called."]]},{"u":"gern-geschehen.html","t":"Gern geschehen.","s":"You're welcome.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Bitte, gern geschehen! :: You're welcome! Bitte schön! :: You're welcome!"],["usage","Usage","The answer to Danke . Shorter: Gern! or Bitte!"]]},{"u":"gern.html","t":"gern","s":"gladly / like to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ja, gern! :: Yes, gladly! Mein Sohn spielt lieber Fußball als Handball. :: My son prefers playing football to handball."],["notes","Notes","Verb + gern says what you like doing: Ich spiele gern Fußball , I like playing football."]]},{"u":"geschichte.html","t":"Geschichte","s":"story","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Liest du mir noch eine Geschichte vor? :: Will you read me a story?"],["notes","Notes","Geschichte is also the school subject history."]]},{"u":"gestern.html","t":"gestern","s":"yesterday","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er hat seit gestern Fieber. :: He has had a fever since yesterday."]]},{"u":"gesund.html","t":"gesund","s":"healthy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er ist wieder gesund und geht morgen in die Schule. :: He is healthy again and is going to school tomorrow."]]},{"u":"gewinnen.html","t":"gewinnen","s":"to win","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hoffentlich gewinnen wir! :: Hopefully we will win! Ihr habt gewonnen! :: You won!"]]},{"u":"gleich.html","t":"gleich","s":"in a moment / right away","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich komme gleich! :: I'm coming!"],["notes","Notes","As an adjective gleich means same : die gleiche Klasse ."]]},{"u":"gluecklich.html","t":"glücklich","s":"happy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach dem Sieg waren alle Kinder glücklich. :: After the win all the children were happy."]]},{"u":"grillen-bei-freunden.html","t":"Grillen bei Freunden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Freund: Wir grillen am Sonntag im Garten. Kommt ihr auch? :: We're having a barbecue in the garden on Sunday. Are you coming too? ich: Sehr gern! Sollen wir etwas mitbringen? :: We'd love to! Should we bring something? Freund: Vielleicht einen Salat? Getränke haben wir genug. :: Maybe a salad? We have enough drinks. ich: Kein Problem, ich mache einen Kartoffelsalat. Können die Kinder auch kommen? :: No problem, I'll make a potato salad. Can the children come too? Freund: Natürlich! Unsere Kinder freuen sich. :: Of course! Our children will be happy. ich: Super. Wann sollen wir da sein? :: Great. When should we be there? Freund: So gegen eins. Bis Sonntag! :: Around one. See you on Sunday!"],["variations","Variations","2 ich: Schade, am Sonntag können wir nicht. Wir haben schon etwas vor. :: Pity, we can't on Sunday. We already have plans."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. etwas vorhaben : to have plans. gegen eins : around one o'clock."]]},{"u":"gross.html","t":"groß","s":"big / tall","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist schon sehr groß. :: My son is already very tall. Unsere Wohnung ist größer als die alte. :: Our flat is bigger than the old one."]]},{"u":"grosseltern.html","t":"Großeltern","s":"grandparents","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Wochenende besuchen wir die Großeltern. :: At the weekend we visit the grandparents."],["notes","Notes","die Oma and der Opa are the everyday words for grandmother and grandfather."]]},{"u":"grundbuch.html","t":"Grundbuch","s":"land register","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bedingung ist, dass Sie im Grundbuch eingetragen sind. :: The condition is that you are registered in the land register. Erforderlicher Nachweis ist ein Grundbuchauszug und eine amtliche Meldebescheinigung. :: The proof required is an extract from the land register and an official certificate of registration. Wir bestellen einen Grundbuchauszug beim Grundbuchamt. :: We are ordering an extract from the land register at the land registry."],["notes","Notes","You are im Grundbuch eingetragen (registered in it) when you own the land. A copy of the entry is a Grundbuchauszug ."]]},{"u":"gruss-am-schultor.html","t":"Gruß am Schultor","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Mutter: Hallo! Na, wie geht's? :: Hi! So, how are you? ich: Hallo! Gut, danke. Und dir? :: Hi! Fine, thanks. And you? Mutter: Ganz gut, aber ein bisschen müde. Kommst du am Donnerstag zum Elternabend? :: Quite well, but a bit tired. Are you coming to the parents' evening on Thursday? ich: Ja, ich komme. Weißt du, wann er anfängt? :: Yes, I'm coming. Do you know when it starts? Mutter: Um halb acht, im Klassenzimmer. :: At half past seven, in the classroom. ich: Super, danke. Bis Donnerstag! :: Great, thanks. See you on Thursday!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Leider nicht, ich muss arbeiten. Kannst du mir danach erzählen, was die Lehrerin sagt? :: Sadly not, I have to work. Can you tell me afterwards what the teacher says?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Parents at the school gate usually say du to each other. Weißt du, wann er anfängt? After wann inside a sentence, the verb goes to the end."]]},{"u":"gut-gemacht.html","t":"Gut gemacht!","s":"Well done!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Weiter so! :: Keep it up! Super gespielt! :: Great game!"],["usage","Usage","To praise a child after training or after homework."]]},{"u":"gut.html","t":"gut","s":"good / well","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ihr habt gut gespielt. :: You played well. Die andere Mannschaft ist besser. :: The other team is better."]]},{"u":"gute-besserung.html","t":"Gute Besserung!","s":"Get well soon!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Gute Besserung an deinen Sohn! :: Get well soon to your son! Gute Besserung für Ihre Tochter! :: Get well soon to your daughter!"],["usage","Usage","What you say to someone who is ill, or about someone who is ill."]]},{"u":"gute-nacht.html","t":"Gute Nacht","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Es ist acht Uhr. Zeit fürs Bett! :: It's eight o'clock. Time for bed! Kind: Schon? Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: Already? May I watch TV for ten more minutes? ich: Nein, morgen ist Schule. Hast du die Zähne geputzt? :: No, there's school tomorrow. Have you brushed your teeth? Kind: Ja. Liest du mir noch eine Geschichte vor? :: Yes. Will you read me a story? ich: Gern, aber nur eine kurze. :: Gladly, but only a short one. Kind: Gute Nacht! Ich hab dich lieb. :: Good night! I love you. ich: Ich dich auch. Schlaf gut! :: Me too. Sleep well!"],["variations","Variations","3 ich: Na gut, zehn Minuten. Aber dann ist Schluss! :: All right, ten minutes. But then that's it!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Ich hab dich lieb is how family members say I love you . Ich liebe dich is for partners."]]},{"u":"haben.html","t":"haben","s":"to have","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du heute Hausaufgaben? :: Do you have homework today? Heute Morgen hatte er 39 Grad. :: This morning he had a temperature of 39 degrees."]]},{"u":"halb.html","t":"halb","s":"half","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: We have to leave at half past seven."],["notes","Notes","halb acht is 7:30: half way to eight, not half past eight."]]},{"u":"halle.html","t":"Halle","s":"sports hall","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid immer 45 Minuten vor dem Spiel in der Halle. :: Please always be in the hall 45 minutes before the match."]]},{"u":"hallo.html","t":"hallo","s":"hello / hi","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hallo! Na, wie geht's? :: Hi! So, how are you?"],["notes","Notes","Informal, to people you know. With Sie : Guten Tag ."]]},{"u":"halt-bei-bedarf.html","t":"Halt bei Bedarf","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","RB [Nummer] [Zugname] [Ort] - [Ort] Hbf 05:54 [Ort] Abfahrt 5:52 Weiterfahrt nach 5:54 [Ort] (Halt bei Bedarf) 6:00 [Ort] Hbf Standort im Zug"],["meaning","Meaning","The display inside a regional train (RB, Regionalbahn). It shows the line, the route and the clock (05:54). The train is at a station and left at 5:52 ( Abfahrt ). It goes on ( Weiterfahrt ) to the next stop at 5:54, where it only stops on request ( Halt bei Bedarf ), and arrives at the main station ( Hbf , Hauptbahnhof ) at 6:00. Standort im Zug shows where you are in the train."]]},{"u":"halten.html","t":"halten","s":"to hold / to save (a ball)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe drei Bälle gehalten. :: I saved three balls."]]},{"u":"halteverbot.html","t":"Halteverbot","s":"no-stopping zone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","An Schultagen ist hier von 7 bis 9 Uhr Halteverbot. :: On school days there is no stopping here from 7 to 9. Das Halteverbot gilt nicht für Linienbusse. :: The no-stopping rule does not apply to scheduled buses."],["notes","Notes","Halten is stopping for up to three minutes, Parken is longer or leaving the car. A red cross on blue is the absolute ban ( absolutes Halteverbot ); a single red stripe is the limited one ( eingeschränktes Halteverbot ), where you may stop for three minutes but not park."]]},{"u":"handball.html","t":"Handball","s":"handball","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter spielt Handball im Verein. :: My daughter plays handball in a club."]]},{"u":"hausaufgabe.html","t":"Hausaufgabe","s":"homework task","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play. Hast du heute Hausaufgaben? :: Do you have homework today?"],["notes","Notes","Mostly used in the plural: Hausaufgaben machen , to do homework."]]},{"u":"hausaufgaben-machen.html","t":"Hausaufgaben machen","s":"to do homework","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Zuerst machst du die Hausaufgaben. :: First you do your homework. Hast du die Hausaufgaben schon gemacht? :: Have you done your homework yet?"],["usage","Usage","German uses machen , not tun , for homework."]]},{"u":"hausaufgaben.html","t":"Hausaufgaben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Wie war's in der Schule? :: How was school? Kind: Gut. Wir haben in Mathe ein Spiel gemacht. :: Good. We played a game in maths. ich: Schön! Hast du heute Hausaufgaben? :: Nice! Do you have homework today? Kind: Ja, Deutsch und Mathe. Aber ich will zuerst spielen. :: Yes, German and maths. But I want to play first. ich: Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play. Kind: Kannst du mir helfen? Die Aufgabe ist so schwer. :: Can you help me? The task is so hard. ich: Na klar. Zeig mal! :: Of course. Show me!"],["variations","Variations","2 Kind: Nicht so gut. Ich habe mein Heft vergessen. :: Not so good. I forgot my exercise book. 7 ich: Jetzt nicht, ich koche gerade. Frag doch deine Schwester. :: Not now, I'm cooking. Why don't you ask your sister."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. dann darfst du spielen : after dann the verb comes right away, in position 2."]]},{"u":"heiss.html","t":"heiß","s":"hot","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Sommer ist es in der Halle sehr heiß. :: In summer it is very hot in the hall."]]},{"u":"helfen.html","t":"helfen","s":"to help","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir helfen? :: Can you help me?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Kannst du mich helfen? :: Kannst du mir helfen?"]]},{"u":"herzlich-willkommen.html","t":"Herzlich willkommen!","s":"Welcome!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Herzlich willkommen im Haus! :: Welcome to the house! Willkommen in der Mannschaft! :: Welcome to the team!"],["usage","Usage","To greet a new neighbour, a new player or the guests of an evening."]]},{"u":"herzlichen-glueckwunsch.html","t":"Herzlichen Glückwunsch!","s":"Congratulations!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Herzlichen Glückwunsch zum Geburtstag! :: Happy birthday! Herzlichen Glückwunsch, ihr habt gewonnen! :: Congratulations, you won!"],["usage","Usage","For a birthday, a win or good news."]]},{"u":"heute.html","t":"heute","s":"today","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist ein besonderer Tag. :: Today is a special day."]]},{"u":"hier.html","t":"hier","s":"here","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wohnen Sie schon lange hier? :: Have you lived here long?"]]},{"u":"hinter.html","t":"hinter","s":"behind","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Mülltonnen stehen hinter dem Haus. :: The bins are behind the house."]]},{"u":"hinzufuegen.html","t":"hinzufügen","s":"to add","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte fügt mich zur WhatsApp-Gruppe hinzu. :: Please add me to the WhatsApp group. Der Trainer hat mich zur Gruppe hinzugefügt. :: The coach added me to the group."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Bitte hinzufügt mich zur Gruppe. :: Bitte fügt mich zur Gruppe hinzu."],["notes","Notes","zu + Dativ for the group: zur Gruppe (zu der Gruppe)."]]},{"u":"hitze.html","t":"Hitze","s":"heat","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kind A. kann heute wegen der großen Hitze nicht zum Training kommen. :: Child A. cannot come to training today because of the great heat. Bei dieser Hitze machen wir nur lockere Übungen. :: In this heat we only do light exercises."],["notes","Notes","hitzefrei is a day off school because of the heat."]]},{"u":"hoch.html","t":"hoch","s":"high","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie hoch ist das Fieber? :: How high is the fever?"],["notes","Notes","Before a noun it loses the c : hohes Fieber ."]]},{"u":"hoffentlich.html","t":"hoffentlich","s":"hopefully","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hoffentlich gewinnen wir! :: Hopefully we'll win!"]]},{"u":"hundert.html","t":"hundert","s":"a hundred","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Ausflug kostet nicht hundert, sondern fünf Euro. :: The trip doesn't cost a hundred but five euros."],["notes","Notes","hundertzwanzig is 120, zweihundert is 200."]]},{"u":"husten.html","t":"Husten","s":"cough","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn hat Husten und kann nicht schlafen. :: My son has a cough and cannot sleep."]]},{"u":"ich-komme-gleich.html","t":"Ich komme gleich!","s":"I'm coming!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Moment, ich komme gleich! :: Just a moment, I'm coming!"],["usage","Usage","gleich means in a moment ."]]},{"u":"ich-muss-los.html","t":"Ich muss los.","s":"I have to go.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","So, ich muss los. :: Right, I have to go. Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: We have to leave at half past seven."],["usage","Usage","A friendly way to end a chat. los stands for losgehen or losfahren ."]]},{"u":"ich.html","t":"ich","s":"I","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir helfen? :: Can you help me? Er ruft mich morgen an. :: He will call me tomorrow."]]},{"u":"ihr.html","t":"ihr","s":"you (plural informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommt ihr auch? :: Are you coming too? Ich bringe euch einen Salat mit. :: I will bring you a salad."]]},{"u":"im-leistungsumfang-enthalten.html","t":"im Leistungsumfang enthalten","s":"included in the scope of services","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ggf. notwendige Erdarbeiten sind nicht im Leistungsumfang enthalten. :: Any earthworks that may be needed are not included in the scope of services. Ist die Entsorgung der Öl-Tanks im Leistungsumfang enthalten? :: Is the disposal of the oil tanks included in the scope of services? Die Wartung ist im Preis enthalten. :: Maintenance is included in the price."],["usage","Usage","Offers and contracts list what the company will do ( der Leistungsumfang ) and what it will not. Look for nicht enthalten before you sign. im Preis inbegriffen means the same in everyday language."]]},{"u":"immer.html","t":"immer","s":"always","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid immer pünktlich. :: Please always be on time."]]},{"u":"imperativ.html","t":"Imperativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Commands and requests. Add bitte to sound friendly. du : the stem, no du : Verbs with Komm ! Räum dein Zimmer auf! Zieh dich an! e to i keep it: Gib mir den Ball! Nimm die Jacke mit! ihr : the ihr form without ihr : Kommt ! Beeilt euch! Sie : the Sie form, verb first: Kommen Sie bitte um elf Uhr. Bringen Sie die Karte mit. sein is special: Sei leise! Seid pünktlich! Seien Sie bitte pünktlich."],["simple-german","Simple German","Imperativ: Komm! (du), Kommt! (ihr), Kommen Sie! (Sie). Mit bitte ist es freundlich."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Du komm bitte! :: Komm bitte! Gebe mir den Ball! :: Gib mir den Ball!"]]},{"u":"in-der-kaffeepause.html","t":"In der Kaffeepause","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Kollegin: Morgen! Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Morning! Would you like a coffee too? ich: Ja, gern. Mit Milch, ohne Zucker, bitte. :: Yes, please. With milk, no sugar. Kollegin: Wie war dein Wochenende? :: How was your weekend? ich: Schön, aber anstrengend. Meine Kinder hatten zwei Spiele. Und deins? :: Nice, but tiring. My children had two matches. And yours? Kollegin: Ruhig. Ich habe viel gelesen und geschlafen. :: Quiet. I read and slept a lot. ich: Das klingt gut! So, ich muss los. Um zehn habe ich eine Besprechung. :: That sounds good! Right, I have to go. At ten I have a meeting. Kollegin: Viel Erfolg! Bis später. :: Good luck! See you later."],["variations","Variations","3 Kollegin: Was hast du am Wochenende gemacht? :: What did you do at the weekend?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Morgen! alone is short for Guten Morgen! . Colleagues often say du ; ask when you are not sure."]]},{"u":"in-der-praxis.html","t":"In der Praxis","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Ärztin: Hallo! Was fehlt dir denn? :: Hello! What's wrong with you? Kind: Mein Hals tut weh. :: My throat hurts. Ärztin: Mach bitte mal den Mund auf. Ah ja, der Hals ist rot. :: Open your mouth, please. Ah yes, the throat is red. ich: Ist es schlimm? :: Is it bad? Ärztin: Nein, das ist nur eine Erkältung. Er soll viel trinken und drei Tage zu Hause bleiben. :: No, it's only a cold. He should drink a lot and stay at home for three days. ich: Braucht er Medikamente? :: Does he need medicine? Ärztin: Ich schreibe Ihnen ein Rezept für einen Fiebersaft. :: I'll write you a prescription for a fever syrup. ich: Brauchen wir eine Bescheinigung für die Schule? :: Do we need a certificate for school? Ärztin: Ja, die bekommen Sie vorne an der Anmeldung. :: Yes, you'll get it at the reception at the front."],["variations","Variations","5 Ärztin: Er hat eine Mittelohrentzündung. Er braucht ein Antibiotikum. :: He has a middle ear infection. He needs an antibiotic."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. The doctor says du to the child and Sie to the parent. For work, ask for the certificate for the employer too: Ich brauche auch eine Bescheinigung für meinen Arbeitgeber."]]},{"u":"in.html","t":"in","s":"in / into","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen in die Halle. :: We are going into the hall. Wir sind in der Halle. :: We are in the hall."],["notes","Notes","in die Halle : where to, Akkusativ. in der Halle : where, Dativ."]]},{"u":"infinitiv-als-nomen.html","t":"Infinitiv als Nomen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Any infinitive can become a noun: capital letter, always neuter ( das ). Signs love it because it names an action without a person. Without an article the adjective takes -es ; in the genitive the noun takes -s . Unbefugtes Betreten und Befahren verboten! :: Entering and driving in without permission forbidden! Unbefugtes Parken auf eigene Gefahr! :: Parking without permission at your own risk! Der Sinn des Wanderns ist, unterwegs zu sein. :: The point of hiking is to be on the way."],["simple-german","Simple German","Aus einem Verb wird ein Nomen: parken wird das Parken . Großer Buchstabe, immer das . Genitiv: des Wanderns ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Das parken ist hier verboten. :: Das Parken ist hier verboten. Unbefugter Betreten verboten! :: Unbefugtes Betreten verboten!"]]},{"u":"infos-spanienfahrt-2027.html","t":"Infos zur Spanienfahrt 2027","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Es ist mal wieder so weit! Unsere Spanienfahrt über Ostern steht mal wieder an und dazu bekommt ihr im Folgenden alle wichtigen Infos! It's that time again! Our Easter trip to Spain is coming up again, and below you get all the important information! Wir werden im nächsten Jahr die Trofeo Mediterraneo besuchen (viel internationalere Mannschaften). Next year we will go to the Trofeo Mediterraneo (many more international teams). Abfahrt: 19.03.2027 abends zwischen 19 und 21 Uhr. Die genaue Abfahrtszeit wird noch bekannt gegeben. Departure: 19.03.2027 in the evening, between 7 and 9 pm. The exact departure time will be announced later. Ankunft: 27.03.2027 / 28.03.2027, nachts ca. 1:00 Uhr. Arrival: 27.03.2027 / 28.03.2027, at night, around 1 am. Abfahrtsort: [Ort]. Aufgrund der großen Anzahl an Teilnehmern, Baustellen usw. wird der Abfahrtsort voraussichtlich verlegt. Place of departure: [Town]. Because of the large number of participants, roadworks and so on, the place of departure will probably be moved. Die Kosten der Fahrt belaufen sich auf 670 € pro Teilnehmer. The trip costs 670 € per participant. Im Preis mit inbegriffen sind Bustransfer nach Spanien und zurück, Bustransfer vor Ort zu den Spielen und das Hotel vor Ort (Vollpension). The price includes the bus to Spain and back, the bus to the matches there and the hotel there (full board). Vollpension heißt Buffet am Morgen, Mittag und Abend. Full board means a buffet in the morning, at midday and in the evening. Im letzten Jahr konnten wir alle sonstigen Aktivitäten vor Ort ohne zusätzliche Kosten für jeden Einzelnen ermöglichen, wie z. B. eine Busfahrt nach Barcelona mit Stadtrundfahrt und Besichtigung des Camp Nou, einen Tag im Aktiv-Camp mit Lasertag und Fußballgolf und einen Teamtag am Strand. Last year we could offer all the other activities there at no extra cost for anyone, for example a bus trip to Barcelona with a city tour and a visit to the Camp Nou, a day at an activity camp with laser tag and footgolf, and a team day at the beach. Das kommt allerdings ganz darauf an, wie viele Sponsoren gefunden werden. However, that depends entirely on how many sponsors are found. Von daher bitten wir alle Eltern, Spieler und Bekannte, ausgiebig nach Sponsoren zu suchen, egal in welcher Form, und auch über kleine Spenden freuen wir uns sehr. So we ask all parents, players and friends to look hard for sponsors, in any form, and we are also very happy about small donations. Bei Fragen oder wenn ihr Erfolg bei der Suche hattet, schreibt gerne Herrn K. oder mich an! If you have questions or if your search was successful, feel free to write to Mr K. or to me! Um nicht ausschließlich auf Spenden und Sponsoren angewiesen zu sein, möchten wir auch selbst aktiv zur Finanzierung beitragen. So as not to depend only on donations and sponsors, we also want to contribute to the funding ourselves. Daher werden wir in diesem Jahr erneut an den Adventssamstagen einen Waffelverkauf vor den örtlichen Einkaufsmärkten organisieren. So this year we will again organise a waffle sale in front of the local supermarkets on the Saturdays of Advent. Zusätzlich findet im Rahmen der Wintervorbereitung Ende Februar wieder ein JSG-Tag statt, an dem alle teilnehmenden Mannschaften ein Spiel ausrichten. In addition, as part of the winter preparation, there will again be a JSG day at the end of February, on which all participating teams host a match. Die daraus erzielten Einnahmen kommen ebenfalls der Spanienfahrt zugute. The money raised from it also goes to the trip to Spain. Auch hierbei freuen wir uns über Unterstützung jeglicher Art. Nähere Informationen hierzu folgen. Here too we welcome support of any kind. More details will follow. Zur Anmeldung: Der Preis von 670 € wird von jedem Mitfahrer selbst per Überweisung getätigt. About registration: each participant pays the price of 670 € themselves by bank transfer. Diese Überweisung gilt als verbindliche Anmeldung und muss bis zum 31.10.2026 auf unten aufgeführtes Konto eingegangen sein. This transfer counts as a binding registration and must have reached the account below by 31.10.2026. Wir haben dieses Jahr zusätzlich die Herausforderung, dass der Veranstalter den Termin zur Anzahlung 2 Monate vorgezogen hat. This year we also have the challenge that the organiser has moved the deposit date forward by 2 months. Entsprechend bitten wir alle, bei denen die Teilnahme bereits klar und möglich ist, die Zahlung bis zum 16.10.2026 auszuführen. Vielen Dank für eure Hilfe. So we ask everyone whose participation is already clear and possible to make the payment by 16.10.2026. Many thanks for your help. Konto: [Verein]. IBAN: [IBAN]. Verwendungszweck: Vorname und Nachname des Kindes und Spanien 2027. Account: [Club]. IBAN: [IBAN]. Payment reference: the child's first name and surname and \"Spanien 2027\". Aus buchhalterischen Gründen bitten wir darum, die Überweisungen einzeln durchzuführen, wenn mehrere Mitfahrer aus einer Familie dabei sind. Fo"],["notes","Notes","The original had two small slips, cleaned up here: die zusätzliche die Herausforderung and mit in vielen unvergesslichen Momenten . The list of activities is written as one sentence. sich belaufen auf is formal for \"to come to, to amount to\": Die Kosten belaufen sich auf 670 €. angewiesen sein auf (+ Akkusativ): to depend on. zugutekommen (+ Dativ): to benefit. Die Einnahmen kommen der Spanienfahrt zugute. wird bekannt gegeben , gefunden werden , wird getätigt : the letter uses the passive a lot. See Passiv mit werden ."]]},{"u":"ins-bett-gehen.html","t":"ins Bett gehen","s":"to go to bed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Um acht Uhr gehen die Kinder ins Bett. :: At eight o'clock the children go to bed. Zeit fürs Bett! :: Time for bed!"],["usage","Usage","ins is in das : movement, so Akkusativ. In bed is im Bett ."]]},{"u":"ja.html","t":"ja","s":"yes","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ja, gern! :: Yes, gladly!"],["notes","Notes","Inside a sentence ja is also a particle that means as you know : Das ist ja toll!"]]},{"u":"jeder.html","t":"jeder","s":"every / each","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Jeden Dienstag ist Training. :: There is training every Tuesday. Jedes Kind bringt eine Flasche Wasser mit. :: Every child brings a bottle of water."],["notes","Notes","Only singular. Endings like der, die, das : jeder, jede, jedes ."]]},{"u":"jemand.html","t":"jemand","s":"somebody","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kann jemand am Samstag fahren? :: Can somebody drive on Saturday?"]]},{"u":"jemanden-in-kenntnis-setzen.html","t":"jemanden in Kenntnis setzen","s":"to inform someone (formal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sie setzen die Firma A unverzüglich nach Zusage der Förderung in Kenntnis. :: You inform company A without delay once the subsidy is approved. Hiermit setze ich Sie in Kenntnis, dass die Förderung bewilligt wurde. :: I hereby inform you that the subsidy has been approved. Bitte setzen Sie uns über jede Änderung in Kenntnis. :: Please inform us of any change."],["usage","Usage","Contracts and official letters use it for informieren or Bescheid geben . The person is in the accusative; what you inform about comes with über or a dass clause. In your own e-mails, ich möchte Ihnen mitteilen, dass ... sounds less stiff."]]},{"u":"jetzt.html","t":"jetzt","s":"now","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir treffen uns jetzt am Dienstag. :: We are now meeting on Tuesday. Jetzt nicht, ich koche gerade. :: Not now, I'm cooking."]]},{"u":"jung.html","t":"jung","s":"young","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Schwester ist jünger als ich. :: My sister is younger than me."]]},{"u":"kaffee.html","t":"Kaffee","s":"coffee","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Would you like a coffee too?"]]},{"u":"kalt.html","t":"kalt","s":"cold","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist es kalt. Zieh die Jacke an! :: It's cold today. Put your jacket on! Mir ist kalt. :: I'm cold."],["notes","Notes","You feel cold with the Dativ: Mir ist kalt , not Ich habe kalt ."]]},{"u":"kaputt.html","t":"kaputt","s":"broken","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Heizung ist kaputt. :: The heating is broken."]]},{"u":"kaufvertrag-waermepumpe-auf-raten.html","t":"Kaufvertrag: Wärmepumpe auf Raten","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Die Firma A finanziert Ihnen den Kauf der Wärmepumpe über einen Ratenkauf. Company A finances your purchase of the heat pump through a hire purchase. Bei dieser Finanzierung müssen Sie den Gesamtkaufpreis nicht sofort zahlen, sondern zahlen diesen zzgl. Zinsen in mehreren vereinbarten monatlichen Raten über eine vereinbarte Laufzeit. With this financing you do not have to pay the total purchase price at once: you pay it plus interest in several agreed monthly instalments over an agreed term. Die Laufzeit beträgt 15 Jahre beginnend mit dem Monat, der auf die Abnahme der Anlage folgt. Die Monatsraten werden zum 5. des jeweiligen Monats fällig. The term is 15 years, starting with the month after the acceptance of the system. The monthly instalments are due on the 5th of each month. Sondertilgungen (auch des gesamten Betrags) sind jederzeit möglich, keine Vorfälligkeitsentschädigung. Extra repayments (even of the whole amount) are possible at any time, with no early repayment penalty. 0 € Anzahlung: Sie zahlen erst nach Installation der Wärmepumpe. No down payment: you only pay after the heat pump has been installed. Die angegebene Förderung ist voraussichtlich und abhängig von Bewilligung sowie Auszahlung durch die KfW. The subsidy stated is an estimate and depends on approval and payment by the KfW. Der volle Gesamtkaufpreis ist an die Firma A zu zahlen; die Förderung erhalten Sie separat direkt von der KfW. The full purchase price must be paid to company A; you receive the subsidy separately, directly from the KfW. Ggf. notwendige Erdarbeiten sind nicht im Leistungsumfang enthalten. Any earthworks that may be needed are not included in the scope of services. Ggf. notwendige Entsorgung vorhandener Öl-Tanks ist nicht im Leistungsumfang enthalten. Any disposal of existing oil tanks that may be needed is not included in the scope of services. Die Montage, Installation und Inbetriebnahme werden voraussichtlich mehrere Tage in Anspruch nehmen. Fitting, installation and commissioning will probably take several days. Die Heizung und die Wasserversorgung auf dem Grundstück bzw. im Gebäude wird während dieses Zeitraums kalt sein. The heating and the water supply on the property or in the building will be cold during this period. Sie bestätigen, dass Sie die Firma A unverzüglich nach Zusage oder Ablehnung der Förderung in Kenntnis setzen und den entsprechenden Bescheid in Kopie übermitteln. You confirm that you will inform company A without delay once the subsidy is approved or refused, and send a copy of the decision. Dieser Kaufvertrag erlischt, sobald und soweit die KfW den Antrag zur Förderung nicht bewilligt, sondern mit einem Ablehnungsschreiben abgelehnt hat (auflösende Bedingung). This purchase contract ends as soon as and to the extent that the KfW does not approve the subsidy application but rejects it with a letter of refusal (condition subsequent). Der Käufer kann seine Vertragserklärung innerhalb von 14 Tagen ohne Angabe von Gründen widerrufen. The buyer can withdraw his contractual declaration within 14 days without giving reasons."],["notes","Notes","Short extracts of a long contract, in the order they appear. The company name is replaced by Firma A ; prices, numbers and the address are left out. zzgl. is zuzüglich (plus), ggf. is gegebenenfalls (if necessary), bzw. is beziehungsweise (or rather). ist ... zu zahlen is sein + zu + Infinitiv : it must be paid. To do: send the company a copy of the KfW approval letter."]]},{"u":"kein-problem.html","t":"Kein Problem!","s":"No problem!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Kein Problem, ich mache einen Salat. :: No problem, I'll make a salad. Das ist kein Problem. :: That's no problem."],["usage","Usage","An easy way to say yes to a request."]]},{"u":"kein.html","t":"kein","s":"no / not a","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe keine Zeit. :: I have no time. Das ist kein Problem. :: That is no problem."],["notes","Notes","kein negates a noun with ein or with no article. Everything else takes nicht ."]]},{"u":"keller.html","t":"Keller","s":"basement / cellar","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Handwerker reparieren die Heizung im Keller. :: The workmen are repairing the heating in the basement."]]},{"u":"kind.html","t":"Kind","s":"child","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Kind geht in die zweite Klasse. :: My child is in second grade. Die Kinder spielen im Garten. :: The children are playing in the garden."]]},{"u":"kinderarzt.html","t":"Kinderarzt","s":"paediatrician","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: We are going to the paediatrician today."],["notes","Notes","A woman is die Kinderärztin . In the practice you mostly talk to the Arzthelferin first."]]},{"u":"klasse.html","t":"Klasse","s":"class / grade","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter geht in die Klasse 2b. :: My daughter is in class 2b."]]},{"u":"klein.html","t":"klein","s":"small / little","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist noch klein. :: My daughter is still little. Am Freitag mache ich eine kleine Party. :: On Friday I'm having a small party."]]},{"u":"koennen.html","t":"können","s":"can / to be able to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir helfen? :: Can you help me? Könnten Sie bitte die Musik leiser machen? :: Could you please turn the music down?"],["notes","Notes","A modal verb: the second verb goes to the end as an infinitive."]]},{"u":"kollegin.html","t":"Kollegin","s":"colleague (woman)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Kollegin trinkt jeden Morgen einen Kaffee mit mir. :: My colleague has a coffee with me every morning."],["notes","Notes","A man is der Kollege , plural die Kollegen ."]]},{"u":"kommen.html","t":"kommen","s":"to come","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommst du am Donnerstag zum Elternabend? :: Are you coming to the parents' evening on Thursday? Ich komme gleich! :: I'm coming!"]]},{"u":"komparativ-und-superlativ.html","t":"Komparativ und Superlativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","To compare: add -er (comparative) and am ...-sten (superlative). Many short words get an umlaut. schnell, schneller, am schnellsten; stark, stärker, am stärksten; krank, kränker, am kränksten Irregular: gut, besser, am besten; gern, lieber, am liebsten; viel, mehr, am meisten . Compare with als : Die andere Mannschaft ist stärker Equal with als wir. so ... wie : Er ist so groß wie sein Bruder."],["simple-german","Simple German","Komparativ mit -er : schneller . Superlativ mit am ...-sten : am schnellsten . Vergleich mit als : besser als ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Er ist mehr schnell. :: Er ist schneller. Sie spielt besser wie ich. :: Sie spielt besser als ich."]]},{"u":"krank.html","t":"krank","s":"ill / sick","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist krank. :: My daughter is ill."]]},{"u":"kunstrasen.html","t":"Kunstrasen","s":"artificial turf, artificial pitch","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist am Sonntag um 11 Uhr auf dem Kunstrasen. :: The match is on Sunday at 11 on the artificial pitch. Auf Kunstrasen braucht man andere Schuhe. :: On artificial turf you need different boots."],["notes","Notes","Kunst (art, artificial) plus Rasen (lawn). The opposite is der Rasenplatz (grass pitch). For several pitches say die Kunstrasenplätze ."]]},{"u":"kurz.html","t":"kurz","s":"short","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Gern, aber nur eine kurze Geschichte. :: Gladly, but only a short story. Haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Do you have a moment?"]]},{"u":"kurze-frage-an-die-lehrerin.html","t":"Kurze Frage an die Lehrerin","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, Frau A., haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Excuse me, Ms A., do you have a moment? Lehrerin: Ja, natürlich. Was gibt's? :: Yes, of course. What is it? ich: Mein Sohn hat morgen einen Termin beim Kinderarzt. Er kommt erst um zehn Uhr in die Schule. :: My son has an appointment at the paediatrician's tomorrow. He will only come to school at ten. Lehrerin: Kein Problem. Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen. :: No problem. Thank you for letting me know. ich: Muss ich eine Entschuldigung schreiben? :: Do I have to write an excuse note? Lehrerin: Ja, bitte geben Sie ihm einen kurzen Zettel mit. :: Yes, please give him a short note to take. ich: Mache ich. Vielen Dank! :: I will. Thank you very much!"],["variations","Variations","6 Lehrerin: Nein, das ist nicht nötig. :: No, that's not necessary."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Teachers are Sie and Frau or Herr with the family name. Frau A. is a placeholder. erst um zehn : erst means not before ."]]},{"u":"laerm.html","t":"Lärm","s":"noise","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach zehn Uhr soll es keinen Lärm geben. :: After ten o'clock there should be no noise."],["notes","Notes","From 22:00 to 6:00 is Nachtruhe : quiet time in most houses."]]},{"u":"lang.html","t":"lang","s":"long","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie lange bleibt sie zu Hause? :: How long will she stay at home? Das Spiel war heute sehr lang. :: The match was very long today."],["notes","Notes","lange (with e ) is the adverb of time: Wohnen Sie schon lange hier?"]]},{"u":"langweilig.html","t":"langweilig","s":"boring","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mathe ist langweilig, sagt mein Sohn. :: Maths is boring, my son says."]]},{"u":"laut.html","t":"laut","s":"loud","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es wird vielleicht ein bisschen laut. :: It might get a bit loud. Ich mache die Musik sofort leiser. :: I will turn the music down right away."],["notes","Notes","The opposite is leise , quiet: leiser machen , to turn down."]]},{"u":"leer.html","t":"leer","s":"empty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Brotdose ist leer. Hast du alles gegessen? :: The lunch box is empty. Did you eat everything?"]]},{"u":"lehrerin.html","t":"Lehrerin","s":"teacher (woman)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Lehrerin hat heute angerufen. :: The teacher called today."],["notes","Notes","A man is der Lehrer , plural die Lehrer . You say Frau A. or Herr B. to a teacher."]]},{"u":"leicht.html","t":"leicht","s":"easy / light","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Hausaufgaben sind heute leicht. :: The homework is easy today."]]},{"u":"leider.html","t":"leider","s":"unfortunately","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Leider nicht, ich muss arbeiten. :: Sadly not, I have to work."]]},{"u":"leise.html","t":"leise","s":"quiet / soft","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid leise, das Baby schläft. :: Please be quiet, the baby is sleeping. Ich mache die Musik sofort leiser. :: I'll turn the music down right away."],["notes","Notes","The opposite is laut . leiser machen : to turn down."]]},{"u":"lernen.html","t":"lernen","s":"to learn / to study","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir lernen heute für den Test. :: Today we are studying for the test."]]},{"u":"lesen.html","t":"lesen","s":"to read","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe viel gelesen und geschlafen. :: I read and slept a lot."]]},{"u":"links.html","t":"links","s":"on the left","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Halle ist hinter der Schule links. :: The hall is behind the school on the left."]]},{"u":"lust-haben.html","t":"Lust haben","s":"to feel like (doing) something","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Hast du Lust auf einen Kaffee? :: Do you fancy a coffee? Hast du Lust, ins Kino zu gehen? :: Do you feel like going to the cinema? Ich habe keine Lust. :: I don't feel like it."],["usage","Usage","To invite a friend, or to say you don't want to. auf plus Akkusativ for a thing; zu plus infinitive for an activity."]]},{"u":"lust.html","t":"Lust","s":"desire / wish","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du Lust auf einen Kaffee? :: Do you fancy a coffee?"],["notes","Notes","Lust haben auf plus Akkusativ: to feel like something."]]},{"u":"lustig.html","t":"lustig","s":"funny","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Film war sehr lustig. :: The film was very funny."]]},{"u":"machen.html","t":"machen","s":"to do / to make","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir haben in Mathe ein Spiel gemacht. :: We played a game in maths. Ich mache einen Kartoffelsalat. :: I will make a potato salad."]]},{"u":"mal.html","t":"mal","s":"just (softens a request)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zeig mal! :: Show me! Mach bitte mal den Mund auf. :: Open your mouth, please."],["notes","Notes","mal makes a request sound friendly and casual."]]},{"u":"man.html","t":"man","s":"one / you / people","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","In der Halle trägt man Hallenschuhe. :: In the hall you wear indoor shoes. Wie sagt man das auf Deutsch? :: How do you say that in German?"],["notes","Notes","man takes the er form of the verb. It is used much more than English one ."]]},{"u":"manchmal.html","t":"manchmal","s":"sometimes","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Manchmal fährt die Oma die Kinder zum Training. :: Sometimes grandma drives the children to training."]]},{"u":"mannschaft.html","t":"Mannschaft","s":"team","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir werden die Trofeo Mediterraneo besuchen, mit viel internationaleren Mannschaften. :: We will go to the Trofeo Mediterraneo, with many more international teams. Alle teilnehmenden Mannschaften richten ein Spiel aus. :: All participating teams host a match. Die andere Mannschaft ist sehr stark. :: The other team is very strong."],["notes","Notes","Feminine because of -schaft . In club language you also hear das Team ."]]},{"u":"mein.html","t":"mein","s":"my","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn spielt Fußball, meine Tochter Handball. :: My son plays football, my daughter handball."],["notes","Notes","Endings like ein . The others: dein, sein, ihr, unser, euer, ihr, Ihr ."]]},{"u":"meistens.html","t":"meistens","s":"mostly / usually","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meistens holen wir die Kinder um vier ab. :: We usually pick up the children at four."]]},{"u":"meldet-euch-gerne.html","t":"meldet euch gerne","s":"feel free to get in touch","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wenn es Probleme mit der Bezahlung gibt, meldet euch gerne. :: If there are problems with the payment, feel free to get in touch. Melde dich gerne, wenn du Fragen hast. :: Get in touch if you have questions. Melden Sie sich gerne bei uns. :: Feel free to contact us. (formal)"],["usage","Usage","sich melden is to get in touch. gerne makes it friendly: \"you are welcome to\". Club messages to parents usually use ihr ."]]},{"u":"mir-gehts-gut.html","t":"Mir geht's gut.","s":"I'm fine.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Gut, danke. Und dir? :: Fine, thanks. And you? Es geht. :: So-so. Nicht so gut. Ich bin erkältet. :: Not so good. I have a cold."],["usage","Usage","The answer to Wie geht's? . mir is Dativ: literally it goes well for me ."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-abhole-meine-tochter.html","t":"Ich abhole meine Tochter","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich abhole meine Tochter um vier."],["right","Right","Ich hole meine Tochter um vier ab."],["why","Why","abholen is separable: the verb is in position 2 and ab goes to the end."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-40-jahre.html","t":"Ich habe 40 Jahre","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe 40 Jahre."],["right","Right","Ich bin 40 Jahre alt."],["why","Why","Age goes with sein : you say how old you are . Spanish tener makes haben come to mind first."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-kalt.html","t":"Ich habe kalt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe kalt."],["right","Right","Mir ist kalt."],["why","Why","Feeling cold or hot is mir ist kalt , mir ist warm , with the person in the Dativ. Spanish says tengo frío ."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-nicht-zeit.html","t":"Ich habe nicht Zeit","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe nicht Zeit."],["right","Right","Ich habe keine Zeit."],["why","Why","A noun without article is negated with kein , not nicht . Spanish no tengo tiempo uses one word for both."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-zum-training-gegangen.html","t":"Ich habe zum Training gegangen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe zum Training gegangen."],["right","Right","Ich bin zum Training gegangen."],["why","Why","gehen is movement from one place to another, so its Perfekt takes sein ."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-spiele-mit-mein-sohn.html","t":"Ich spiele mit mein Sohn","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich spiele mit mein Sohn Fußball."],["right","Right","Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn Fußball."],["why","Why","mit always takes the Dativ: mein becomes meinem for der and das words."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-warte-fuer-dich.html","t":"Ich warte für dich","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich warte für dich vor der Halle."],["right","Right","Ich warte vor der Halle auf dich."],["why","Why","warten takes auf plus Akkusativ. Spanish esperar needs no preposition, English uses for ."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-weiss-nicht-wann-beginnt-das-spiel.html","t":"Ich weiß nicht, wann beginnt das Spiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich weiß nicht, wann beginnt das Spiel."],["right","Right","Ich weiß nicht, wann das Spiel beginnt."],["why","Why","Inside a sentence, after a question word, the verb goes to the end, as after weil and dass ."]]},{"u":"mistake-morgen-ich-gehe-zum-training.html","t":"Morgen ich gehe zum Training","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Morgen ich gehe zum Training."],["right","Right","Morgen gehe ich zum Training."],["why","Why","The verb is always in position 2. When the sentence starts with a time, the subject comes after the verb."]]},{"u":"mit.html","t":"mit","s":"with","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn Fußball. :: I play football with my son."]]},{"u":"mitbringen.html","t":"mitbringen","s":"to bring along","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sollen wir etwas mitbringen? :: Should we bring something? Bitte bringt eure Zahlen vom Oktober mit. :: Please bring your figures from October."]]},{"u":"mitgeben.html","t":"mitgeben","s":"to give someone something to take","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie ihm einen Zettel mit. :: Please give him a note to take."]]},{"u":"mitkommen.html","t":"mitkommen","s":"to come along","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich kann gern als Begleitung mitkommen. :: I can come along as a helper."]]},{"u":"mitnehmen.html","t":"mitnehmen","s":"to take along","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du meine Tochter mitnehmen? :: Can you take my daughter along?"]]},{"u":"mitspielen.html","t":"mitspielen","s":"to play (in a team) / to join in","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kann er am Samstag mitspielen? :: Can he play on Saturday?"]]},{"u":"modalverben.html","t":"Modalverben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","können, müssen, dürfen, wollen, sollen and möchten say whether you can, must, may or want to do something. The modal verb is in position 2; the other verb goes to the end as an infinitive. Ich kann heute nicht kommen . Du darfst noch zehn Minuten fernsehen . Wir müssen um halb acht los . ich and er/sie have the same form and no ending: ich kann, er kann; ich muss, sie muss ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Das Modalverb steht auf Position 2, das zweite Verb am Ende: Ich muss heute arbeiten. Bei ich und er gibt es keine Endung: ich kann, er kann ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich kann kommen nicht. :: Ich kann nicht kommen. Er kannt gut spielen. :: Er kann gut spielen."]]},{"u":"moegen.html","t":"mögen","s":"to like","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn mag Pizza. :: My son likes pizza. Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Would you like a coffee too?"],["notes","Notes","möchte (ich möchte, du möchtest, er möchte) is the polite would like and is used every day."]]},{"u":"morgen.html","t":"morgen","s":"tomorrow","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgen gehe ich zum Training. :: Tomorrow I am going to training."],["notes","Notes","morgen is tomorrow. der Morgen is the morning: heute Morgen , this morning."]]},{"u":"morgens-vor-der-schule.html","t":"Morgens vor der Schule","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Guten Morgen! Aufstehen, es ist schon sieben Uhr. :: Good morning! Get up, it is already seven o'clock. Kind: Ich bin noch so müde. Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: I am still so tired. Five more minutes, please! ich: Nein, keine Zeit. Zieh dich bitte an! Dann komm frühstücken. :: No, no time. Please get dressed! Then come and have breakfast. Kind: Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast? ich: Brot mit Käse und einen Apfel. Hast du deine Brotdose? :: Bread with cheese and an apple. Do you have your lunch box? Kind: Ja, sie ist im Schulranzen. :: Yes, it is in the school bag. ich: Gut. Putz noch schnell die Zähne. Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: Good. Quickly brush your teeth. We have to leave at half past seven. Kind: Okay, ich komme gleich! :: OK, I'm coming!"],["variations","Variations","2 Kind: Mir ist schlecht. Ich will heute nicht in die Schule. :: I feel sick. I don't want to go to school today. 6 Kind: Nein, ich finde sie nicht! :: No, I can't find it!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. halb acht is 7:30: half way to eight. los müssen means to have to leave. Zieh dich an and komm are commands to a child: the Imperativ with du ."]]},{"u":"muede.html","t":"müde","s":"tired","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin noch so müde. :: I am still so tired."]]},{"u":"muell.html","t":"Müll","s":"rubbish","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Mittwoch kommt die Müllabfuhr. :: The rubbish collection comes on Wednesday."],["notes","Notes","Germans separate rubbish: paper, packaging, organic waste and the rest."]]},{"u":"muessen.html","t":"müssen","s":"must / to have to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: We have to leave at half past seven. Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. :: I have to work until six."],["notes","Notes","nicht müssen means not have to : Du musst nicht kommen , you don't have to come."]]},{"u":"mutter.html","t":"Mutter","s":"mother","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute fährt die Mutter von einem Freund die Kinder zum Training. :: Today the mother of a friend drives the children to training."]]},{"u":"na-klar.html","t":"Na klar!","s":"Of course!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ja, klar! :: Yes, sure! Natürlich! :: Of course!"],["usage","Usage","A friendly yes . With people you say Sie to, Natürlich or Gern sounds better."]]},{"u":"na.html","t":"na","s":"well / so","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Na, wie geht's? :: So, how are you? Na ja. Noch fünf Minuten. :: Oh well. Five more minutes."],["notes","Notes","A friendly filler between people who know each other. Na klar! means of course! ."]]},{"u":"nach-dem-spiel.html","t":"Nach dem Spiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Herzlichen Glückwunsch! Ihr habt gewonnen! :: Congratulations! You won! Kind: Ja! Ich habe drei Bälle gehalten. :: Yes! I saved three balls. ich: Ich habe es gesehen. Du warst super! :: I saw it. You were great! Kind: Aber am Ende war ich sehr müde. :: But at the end I was very tired. ich: Das glaube ich. Hast du Hunger? :: I believe it. Are you hungry? Kind: Ja, großen Hunger! Können wir Pizza essen? :: Yes, really hungry! Can we eat pizza? ich: Okay, heute ist ein besonderer Tag. :: OK, today is a special day."],["variations","Variations","1 ich: Schade, ihr habt verloren. Aber ihr habt gut gespielt. :: Pity, you lost. But you played well."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Hunger haben : to be hungry. German uses haben here, like Spanish tener hambre ."]]},{"u":"nach-dem-training.html","t":"Nach dem Training","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Hallo! Wie war das Training heute? :: Hi! How was training today? Trainer: Super! Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Great! Your son scored two goals. ich: Wirklich? Das freut mich! :: Really? I'm glad! Trainer: Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel. Kann er mitspielen? :: On Saturday we have a match. Can he play? ich: Ja, klar. Wann und wo ist das Spiel? :: Yes, sure. When and where is the match? Trainer: Um zehn Uhr auf unserem Platz. Er soll um halb zehn da sein. :: At ten o'clock on our pitch. He should be there at half past nine. ich: Okay. Muss er etwas mitbringen? :: OK. Does he have to bring anything? Trainer: Nur Schienbeinschoner, Fußballschuhe und eine Flasche Wasser. Das Trikot bekommt er von uns. :: Just shin pads, football boots and a bottle of water. He gets the shirt from us."],["variations","Variations","5 ich: Leider nicht, wir besuchen am Wochenende die Großeltern. :: Sadly not, we are visiting the grandparents at the weekend."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. In many clubs the coach and the parents say du to each other. Schienbeinschoner (shin pads) are required in every match."]]},{"u":"nach.html","t":"nach","s":"after / to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach dem Training essen wir zusammen. :: After training we eat together."],["notes","Notes","nach Hause : home (where to). nach also goes with towns and countries: nach Berlin ."]]},{"u":"nachbar.html","t":"Nachbar","s":"neighbour","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Nachbarn feiern am Samstag eine Party. :: Our neighbours are having a party on Saturday."],["notes","Notes","A woman is die Nachbarin , plural die Nachbarinnen ."]]},{"u":"nah.html","t":"nah","s":"near / close","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Schule ist ganz nah. :: The school is very close. Die nächste Haltestelle ist am Marktplatz. :: The nearest stop is on the market square."],["notes","Notes","nächste also means next : nächste Woche , next week."]]},{"u":"natuerlich.html","t":"natürlich","s":"of course / naturally","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Natürlich, das ist kein Problem. :: Of course, that's no problem."]]},{"u":"neben.html","t":"neben","s":"next to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Sportplatz ist neben der Schule. :: The sports ground is next to the school."]]},{"u":"nebensatz-mit-weil-dass-wenn.html","t":"Nebensatz mit weil, dass, wenn","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","After weil (because), dass (that), wenn (if, when) and ob (whether), the conjugated verb goes to the end of the clause. A comma always separates the two clauses. Ich rufe an, weil meine Tochter krank ist . Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen . Ich weiß nicht, ob er heute mitspielen kann . Question words work the same way inside a sentence: Weißt du, wann das Spiel anfängt ? When the subordinate clause comes first, the main clause starts with its verb: Wenn es regnet, fällt das Training aus."],["simple-german","Simple German","Nach weil, dass, wenn, ob steht das Verb am Ende: ..., weil ich arbeiten muss."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich komme nicht, weil ich muss arbeiten. :: Ich komme nicht, weil ich arbeiten muss. Ich weiß nicht, wann beginnt das Spiel. :: Ich weiß nicht, wann das Spiel beginnt."]]},{"u":"nein.html","t":"nein","s":"no","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nein, keine Zeit. :: No, no time."],["notes","Notes","To say yes to a negative question, use doch ."]]},{"u":"nett.html","t":"nett","s":"kind / nice","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: That is very kind of you."]]},{"u":"neu.html","t":"neu","s":"new","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin die neue Nachbarin. :: I'm the new neighbour. Mein Sohn braucht neue Fußballschuhe. :: My son needs new football boots."]]},{"u":"neun.html","t":"neun","s":"nine","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Treffpunkt ist um neun Uhr am Vereinsheim. :: The meeting point is at nine o'clock at the clubhouse."]]},{"u":"nicht-oder-kein.html","t":"Nicht oder kein","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","kein negates a noun that would have ein or no article: Ich habe keine Zeit. Das ist kein Problem. Wir haben keinen Ball. nicht negates everything else: verbs, adjectives, names and nouns with der, die, das : Ich komme nicht . Das Training ist nicht heute. Das ist nicht der Trainer."],["simple-german","Simple German","kein vor Nomen ohne Artikel oder mit ein : keine Zeit . Sonst nicht : Ich komme nicht."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe nicht Zeit. :: Ich habe keine Zeit. Das ist nicht ein Problem. :: Das ist kein Problem."]]},{"u":"nicht.html","t":"nicht","s":"not","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich komme heute nicht. :: I'm not coming today. Das ist nicht schlimm. :: That's not bad."],["notes","Notes","nicht negates verbs, adjectives and nouns with der, die, das . A noun with ein or no article takes kein ."]]},{"u":"nichts.html","t":"nichts","s":"nothing","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das macht nichts. :: It doesn't matter. Ich habe nichts gehört. :: I didn't hear anything."]]},{"u":"nie.html","t":"nie","s":"never","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn räumt nie sein Zimmer auf. :: My son never tidies his room."]]},{"u":"niemand.html","t":"niemand","s":"nobody","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Niemand hat die Sporttasche gesehen. :: Nobody has seen the sports bag."]]},{"u":"noch.html","t":"noch","s":"still / yet / more","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin noch so müde. :: I'm still so tired. Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: Five more minutes, please!"],["notes","Notes","noch nicht : not yet. noch einmal : once more."]]},{"u":"nur.html","t":"nur","s":"only / just","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nur Schienbeinschoner, Fußballschuhe und eine Flasche Wasser. :: Just shin pads, football boots and a bottle of water."]]},{"u":"ob.html","t":"ob","s":"whether / if","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir Bescheid sagen, ob ihr kommt? :: Can you let me know whether you are coming?"],["notes","Notes","ob for a yes-or-no question inside a sentence; wenn for a condition."]]},{"u":"oben.html","t":"oben","s":"upstairs / above","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die neue Nachbarin wohnt oben im zweiten Stock. :: The new neighbour lives upstairs on the second floor."]]},{"u":"oder.html","t":"oder","s":"or","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Spielst du Fußball oder Handball? :: Do you play football or handball?"]]},{"u":"oft.html","t":"oft","s":"often","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir grillen im Sommer oft mit Freunden. :: In summer we often have barbecues with friends."]]},{"u":"oh.html","t":"oh","s":"oh","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Oh, gute Besserung! :: Oh, get well soon!"]]},{"u":"ohne.html","t":"ohne","s":"without","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mit Milch, ohne Zucker, bitte. :: With milk, no sugar, please."]]},{"u":"paket.html","t":"Paket","s":"parcel","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. :: I have a parcel for you."]]},{"u":"passiv-mit-werden.html","t":"Passiv mit werden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Club and school messages use the passive when what happens matters more than who does it : werden plus the participle at the end. With a modal verb, the modal is conjugated and werden goes to the end as an infinitive. Die Abfahrtszeit wird noch bekannt gegeben. :: The departure time will still be announced. Das Spiel wurde verschoben. :: The match was postponed. Das Spiel musste verschoben werden. :: The match had to be postponed. Without a subject, the passive says only that something happens: es wird or a word like hier comes first. Leider wird hier oft sehr schnell gefahren. :: Sadly, people often drive very fast here."],["simple-german","Simple German","Passiv: werden + Partizip. Wichtig ist, was passiert, nicht wer es macht. Mit Modalverb: muss ... verschoben werden ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Das Spiel musste verschoben wird. :: Das Spiel musste verschoben werden. Die Zeit wird bekannt geben. :: Die Zeit wird bekannt gegeben."]]},{"u":"pause.html","t":"Pause","s":"break","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","In der Pause essen die Kinder ihr Frühstück. :: In the break the children eat their snack."]]},{"u":"perfekt-mit-haben-oder-sein.html","t":"Perfekt mit haben oder sein","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The Perfekt is the past tense of conversation: haben or sein in position 2, the participle at the end. Ich habe gestern Fußball gespielt . Wir sind mit dem Bus gefahren . Verbs of movement from one place to another and of change of state take sein : gehen, kommen, fahren, aufstehen, bleiben , and sein itself. Most others take haben . Participles: regular ge-...-t ( gespielt, gemacht ), irregular ge-...-en ( gegangen, geschossen ); no ge- for verbs in -ieren and with be- , ver- : trainiert, besucht, verloren ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Perfekt: haben oder sein plus Partizip am Ende. Bewegung oder Veränderung: mit sein : Ich bin gegangen. Sonst mit haben : Ich habe gespielt."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe zum Training gegangen. :: Ich bin zum Training gegangen. Wir haben gewinnt. :: Wir haben gewonnen."]]},{"u":"personalpronomen.html","t":"Personalpronomen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Nominativ Akkusativ Dativ ich mich mir du dich dir er ihn ihm sie sie ihr es es ihm wir uns uns ihr euch euch sie / Sie sie / Sie ihnen / Ihnen Ich rufe (Akkusativ, dich an anrufen ). Ich helfe (Dativ, dir helfen ). Gib mir den Ball! er and sie also stand for things: der Ball, . er ist weg; die Brotdose, ich finde sie nicht"],["simple-german","Simple German","ich, mich, mir; du, dich, dir; er, ihn, ihm; sie, sie, ihr . Nach anrufen : Akkusativ. Nach helfen : Dativ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Kannst du mich helfen? :: Kannst du mir helfen? Ich rufe ihm an. :: Ich rufe ihn an."]]},{"u":"platz.html","t":"Platz","s":"pitch / seat / square","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist um zehn Uhr auf unserem Platz. :: The match is at ten o'clock on our pitch. Ich habe drei Plätze frei. :: I have three free seats."]]},{"u":"possessivartikel.html","t":"Possessivartikel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Possessive articles say whose something is. They take the endings of ein . ich: mein , du: dein , er: sein , sie: ihr , wir: unser , ihr: euer , sie: ihr , Sie: Ihr mein Sohn, meine Tochter, mein Kind, meine Kinder. Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn. sein belongs to a man, ihr to a woman, whatever the gender of the thing: Sie holt ihren Sohn ab."],["simple-german","Simple German","mein, dein, sein, ihr, unser, euer, Ihr haben die Endungen von ein : meine Tochter, meinen Sohn ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Sie holt seinen Sohn ab. :: Sie holt ihren Sohn ab. Mein Tochter ist krank. :: Meine Tochter ist krank."]]},{"u":"praesens.html","t":"Präsens","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The present tense: take the stem ( spiel- ) and add the ending for the person. ich spiel e , du spiel st , er/sie spiel t , wir spiel en , ihr spiel t , sie/Sie spiel en Some irregular verbs change their vowel with du and er/sie : fahren, du fährst ; helfen, du hilfst ; lesen, du liest . Stems that end in -t or -d add an e : du arbeitest, er wartet . The present tense also speaks about the future when a time is given: Morgen rufe ich dich an."],["simple-german","Simple German","Präsens: Stamm plus Endung: -e, -st, -t, -en, -t, -en . Manche Verben ändern den Vokal bei du und er : du fährst, er hilft ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Du fahrst zum Training. :: Du fährst zum Training. Er arbeit viel. :: Er arbeitet viel."]]},{"u":"praeteritum-von-sein-und-haben.html","t":"Präteritum von sein und haben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","For sein , haben and the modal verbs, Germans use the Präteritum in speech instead of the Perfekt. sein : ich war, du warst, er war, wir waren, ihr wart, sie waren haben : ich hatte, du hattest, er hatte, wir hatten, ihr hattet, sie hatten Wie war dein Wochenende? Heute Morgen hatte er Fieber. Ich konnte nicht kommen."],["simple-german","Simple German","sein und haben in der Vergangenheit: ich war, ich hatte . Man sagt Ich war krank , nicht Ich bin krank gewesen ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wie ist dein Wochenende gewesen? :: Wie war dein Wochenende?"]]},{"u":"privatgrundstueck.html","t":"Privatgrundstück","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Privatgrundstück Unbefugtes Betreten und Befahren verboten! Unbefugtes Parken auf eigene Gefahr! Eingeschränkter Winterdienst! [Landkreis]"],["meaning","Meaning","Private property. Entering on foot or by car without permission is forbidden. If you park here without permission, you do so at your own risk: the owner is not responsible for damage and may have your car towed. The snow and ice are only partly cleared in winter ( Winterdienst is the clearing service)."]]},{"u":"puenktlich.html","t":"pünktlich","s":"on time / punctual","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid immer pünktlich. :: Please always be on time. Der Bus ist heute nicht pünktlich. :: The bus is not on time today."]]},{"u":"putzen.html","t":"putzen","s":"to clean / to brush","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du die Zähne geputzt? :: Have you brushed your teeth?"]]},{"u":"rechts.html","t":"rechts","s":"on the right","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Anmeldung ist vorne rechts. :: The reception is at the front on the right."]]},{"u":"reflexive-verben.html","t":"Reflexive Verben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Some verbs need a reflexive pronoun: the action goes back to the subject. mich, dich, sich, uns, euch, sich Ich ziehe mich an. Zieh dich an! Wir treffen uns um drei. Die Kinder freuen sich . Common ones: sich anziehen, sich beeilen, sich freuen, sich treffen, sich ausruhen, sich anmelden ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Reflexive Verben haben ein Pronomen: ich freue mich, du freust dich, er freut sich ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich freue auf das Spiel. :: Ich freue mich auf das Spiel. Wir treffen um drei. :: Wir treffen uns um drei."]]},{"u":"reservierung-waermepumpe-foerderung-und-vollmacht.html","t":"Reservierung einer Wärmepumpe: Förderung und Vollmacht","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Der Kunde reserviert hiermit ein Wärmepumpensystem für das Gebäude auf dem Grundstück [Adresse]. The customer hereby reserves a heat pump system for the building on the property [address]. Bitte prüfen Sie die nachstehenden förderrelevanten Angaben gründlich. Sie dienen als Grundlage des Angebotes und der Förderung. Please check the following details relevant to the subsidy carefully. They are the basis of the offer and of the subsidy. Bedingung ist, dass Sie im Grundbuch eingetragen sind und der Bauantrag zum Zeitpunkt der Antragsstellung mindestens 5 Jahre zurückliegt. The condition is that you are registered in the land register and that the building application was made at least 5 years before the subsidy application. Bedingung ist, dass Sie als Eigentümer die Wohneinheit zum Zeitpunkt der Antragsstellung als Haupt- bzw. alleinige Wohnung bewohnen. The condition is that, as the owner, you live in the dwelling as your main or only home at the time of the application. Erforderlicher Nachweis ist ein Grundbuchauszug und eine amtliche Meldebescheinigung. The proof required is an extract from the land register and an official certificate of registration. Ich werde für den Erwerb und den Einbau der Wärmepumpe auch keinen Antrag auf steuerliche oder sonstige Förderung stellen. I will also not apply for any tax or other subsidy for the purchase and installation of the heat pump. Die Parteien bevollmächtigen sich gegen- und wechselseitig, in ihrem Namen Erklärungen gegenüber der Firma A abzugeben sowie entgegenzunehmen. The parties authorise each other to make and receive declarations to and from company A in their name. Diese Vollmacht tritt mit Unterzeichnung in Kraft und bleibt bis zu ihrem ausdrücklichen Widerruf in Schriftform gegenüber der Firma A gültig. This power of attorney comes into force when it is signed and stays valid until it is expressly revoked in writing to company A."],["notes","Notes","Extracts of a reservation signed before the contract. The company name is replaced by Firma A and the address by a placeholder; prices and personal data are left out. Antrag stellen and beantragen mean the same: to apply. in Kraft treten : to come into force. Widerruf is the noun of widerrufen ."]]},{"u":"rezept.html","t":"Rezept","s":"prescription / recipe","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich schreibe Ihnen ein Rezept für einen Saft. :: I will write you a prescription for a syrup."]]},{"u":"richtig.html","t":"richtig","s":"right / correct","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ist die Antwort richtig? :: Is the answer right? Doch, der Schiedsrichter hat recht. :: Yes he does, the referee is right."],["notes","Notes","A person is right with recht haben , not richtig ."]]},{"u":"ruhig.html","t":"ruhig","s":"quiet / calm","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Haus ist sehr ruhig. :: The house is very quiet."]]},{"u":"sauber.html","t":"sauber","s":"clean","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Trikot ist wieder sauber. :: The shirt is clean again."]]},{"u":"schade.html","t":"Schade!","s":"What a pity!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Schade, ihr habt verloren. :: Pity, you lost. Das ist aber schade! :: That's a real pity!"],["usage","Usage","When something did not work out."]]},{"u":"schiedsrichter.html","t":"Schiedsrichter","s":"referee","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Schiedsrichter hat recht. :: The referee is right."]]},{"u":"schiessen.html","t":"schießen","s":"to shoot","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Your son scored two goals."],["notes","Notes","ein Tor schießen : to score a goal."]]},{"u":"schlafen.html","t":"schlafen","s":"to sleep","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schlaf gut! :: Sleep well! Meine Kinder können nicht schlafen. :: My children cannot sleep."]]},{"u":"schlimm.html","t":"schlimm","s":"bad / serious","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ist es schlimm? :: Is it bad? Nicht so schlimm! :: Never mind!"]]},{"u":"schmutzig.html","t":"schmutzig","s":"dirty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach dem Training sind die Schuhe immer schmutzig. :: After training the boots are always dirty."]]},{"u":"schnell.html","t":"schnell","s":"fast / quick","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Putz noch schnell die Zähne. :: Quickly brush your teeth."]]},{"u":"schoen.html","t":"schön","s":"nice / beautiful","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schön, dass Sie alle da sind. :: Nice that you are all here. Einen schönen Tag noch! :: Have a nice day!"]]},{"u":"schoenes-wochenende.html","t":"Schönes Wochenende!","s":"Have a nice weekend!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Danke, gleichfalls! :: Thanks, you too! Einen schönen Tag noch! :: Have a nice day!"],["usage","Usage","Said on Friday at work or at the school gate. The answer is Danke, gleichfalls!"]]},{"u":"schon.html","t":"schon","s":"already","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist schon sieben Uhr. :: It is already seven o'clock."]]},{"u":"schule.html","t":"Schule","s":"school","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie war's in der Schule? :: How was school? Morgen ist Schule. :: There is school tomorrow."]]},{"u":"schulranzen.html","t":"Schulranzen","s":"school bag","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Brotdose ist im Schulranzen. :: The lunch box is in the school bag."],["notes","Notes","In the first school years German children carry a Schulranzen on their back."]]},{"u":"schwer.html","t":"schwer","s":"difficult / heavy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Aufgabe ist so schwer. :: The task is so hard."],["notes","Notes","The opposite is leicht : easy, light."]]},{"u":"schwester.html","t":"Schwester","s":"sister","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Schwester hat zwei Kinder. :: My sister has two children."]]},{"u":"sechs.html","t":"sechs","s":"six","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. :: We start at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"sehr.html","t":"sehr","s":"very / very much","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: That's very kind of you."]]},{"u":"sein-zu-infinitiv.html","t":"sein + zu + Infinitiv","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Contracts and official letters say what must (or can ) be done with sein + zu + infinitive at the end. It works like a passive with müssen or können : nobody is named. With a separable verb, zu goes between the prefix and the verb: abzugeben . Der volle Gesamtkaufpreis ist an die Firma A zu zahlen. :: The full purchase price must be paid to company A. Über die Abnahme ist ein Protokoll zu erstellen. :: A record must be made of the acceptance. Die Lieferung ist vom Kunden auf einem Lieferschein zu bestätigen. :: The delivery must be confirmed by the customer on a delivery note. Das Formular ist bis Freitag abzugeben. :: The form must be handed in by Friday."],["simple-german","Simple German","ist ... zu zahlen = muss bezahlt werden . Man sagt nicht, wer es macht."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Der Preis ist an die Firma zu gezahlt. :: Der Preis ist an die Firma zu zahlen. Das Formular ist bis Freitag zu abgeben. :: Das Formular ist bis Freitag abzugeben."]]},{"u":"sein.html","t":"sein","s":"to be","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist krank. :: My daughter is ill. Du warst super! :: You were great!"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe 40 Jahre. :: Ich bin 40 Jahre alt."]]},{"u":"seit.html","t":"seit","s":"since / for","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir wohnen seit drei Jahren hier. :: We have lived here for three years."],["notes","Notes","German uses the present tense with seit where English uses have been ."]]},{"u":"sekretariat.html","t":"Sekretariat","s":"school office","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich rufe im Sekretariat an, wenn mein Kind krank ist. :: I call the school office when my child is ill."]]},{"u":"sich.html","t":"sich","s":"oneself / each other","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Kinder freuen sich. :: The children are happy. Die Eltern treffen sich am Donnerstag. :: The parents meet on Thursday."],["notes","Notes","The reflexive pronoun of er, sie, es, sie (plural) and Sie . The others are mich, dich, uns, euch ."]]},{"u":"sie.html","t":"sie","s":"she / it / they","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I will pick her up at quarter past four."],["notes","Notes","With a capital letter, Sie is the polite you : Können Sie mir helfen? Its Dativ is Ihnen ."]]},{"u":"sieben.html","t":"sieben","s":"seven","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie ist die Nummer sieben, im Tor. :: She is number seven, in goal."],["notes","Notes","Not to be confused with the verb sieben (to sieve), which you will hardly need."]]},{"u":"situation-am-schultor.html","t":"Am Schultor","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Short talks with other parents and the teacher when you bring or pick up your child."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann andere Eltern begrüßen und fragen, wie es ihnen geht. :: I can greet other parents and ask how they are. Ich kann die Lehrerin kurz etwas fragen. :: I can ask the teacher a quick question. Ich kann sagen, dass mein Kind später kommt oder früher geht. :: I can say that my child is coming later or leaving earlier."]]},{"u":"situation-bei-der-arbeit.html","t":"Bei der Arbeit","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Small talk with colleagues and short requests to the boss."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann in der Kaffeepause über das Wochenende sprechen. :: I can talk about the weekend in the coffee break. Ich kann fragen, ob ich früher gehen kann. :: I can ask whether I can leave earlier. Ich kann eine kurze E-Mail über einen Termin verstehen. :: I can understand a short email about a meeting."]]},{"u":"situation-beim-kinderarzt.html","t":"Beim Kinderarzt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Getting an appointment and talking to the paediatrician when a child is ill."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann am Telefon einen Termin vereinbaren. :: I can make an appointment on the phone. Ich kann sagen, was mein Kind hat und seit wann. :: I can say what is wrong with my child and since when. Ich kann fragen, was wir tun sollen und ob wir ein Rezept bekommen. :: I can ask what we should do and whether we get a prescription."]]},{"u":"situation-elternabend.html","t":"Elternabend","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","The evening meeting of the parents of a class with the teacher, a few times a year."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann auf eine Einladung antworten. :: I can reply to an invitation. Ich kann eine Frage zum Ausflug stellen. :: I can ask a question about the trip. Ich kann meine Hilfe anbieten. :: I can offer my help."]]},{"u":"situation-fussballspiel.html","t":"Fußballspiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann verstehen, wann und wo das Treffen vor dem Spiel ist. :: I can understand when and where the meeting before the match is. Ich kann verstehen, dass ein Spiel verschoben wurde und wann der neue Termin ist. :: I can understand that a match was postponed and when the new date is. Ich kann fragen, ob mein Sohn am Wochenende spielt. :: I can ask whether my son is playing at the weekend."]]},{"u":"situation-fussballtraining.html","t":"Fußballtraining","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann dem Trainer schreiben, dass mein Sohn heute nicht zum Training kommt. :: I can write to the coach that my son is not coming to training today. Ich kann fragen, wann die Kinder zum Training da sein sollen. :: I can ask when the children should be at training. Ich kann eine Nachricht des Trainers in der WhatsApp-Gruppe verstehen. :: I can understand a message from the coach in the WhatsApp group. Ich kann den Trainer fragen, wie das Training war. :: I can ask the coach how training was. Ich kann fragen, wann und wo das nächste Spiel ist. :: I can ask when and where the next match is. Ich kann eine Fahrgemeinschaft mit anderen Eltern organisieren. :: I can organise a lift share with other parents."]]},{"u":"situation-handballspiel.html","t":"Handballspiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Handball matches at the weekend: on the stand with other parents and with your child after the game."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann auf der Tribüne über das Spiel sprechen. :: I can talk about the match on the stand. Ich kann nach dem Spiel gratulieren oder trösten. :: I can congratulate or comfort after the match. Ich kann den Spielplan lesen. :: I can read the match schedule."]]},{"u":"situation-heizungstausch.html","t":"Heizungstausch","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann die wichtigsten Punkte im Kaufvertrag verstehen: Raten, Abnahme und Förderung. :: I can understand the main points of the purchase contract: instalments, acceptance and subsidy. Ich kann den Monteuren den Heizungsraum und den Zählerschrank zeigen. :: I can show the fitters the boiler room and the meter cabinet. Ich kann fragen, wie lange die Montage dauert und wann die Abnahme ist. :: I can ask how long the installation takes and when the acceptance is. Ich kann der Firma mitteilen, dass die Förderung bewilligt ist. :: I can tell the company that the subsidy has been approved."]]},{"u":"situation-im-treppenhaus.html","t":"Im Treppenhaus","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Meeting the neighbours in the stairwell: greetings, parcels, noise and notes on the wall."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann mich einer neuen Nachbarin vorstellen. :: I can introduce myself to a new neighbour. Ich kann ein Paket für die Nachbarn annehmen und abgeben. :: I can accept a parcel for the neighbours and hand it over. Ich kann höflich sagen, dass etwas zu laut ist. :: I can say politely that something is too loud. Ich kann einen Zettel der Hausverwaltung verstehen. :: I can understand a note from the property management."]]},{"u":"situation-kind-krank-melden.html","t":"Kind krank melden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Calling the school office in the morning when your child is ill."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann am Telefon sagen, wer ich bin und in welche Klasse mein Kind geht. :: I can say on the phone who I am and which class my child is in. Ich kann sagen, was mein Kind hat und wie lange es zu Hause bleibt. :: I can say what is wrong with my child and how long they will stay at home. Ich kann mich am Telefon verabschieden. :: I can say goodbye on the phone."]]},{"u":"situation-mannschaftsfahrt.html","t":"Mannschaftsfahrt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann die Infos zur Fahrt verstehen: Abfahrt, Kosten, Anmeldung. :: I can understand the trip information: departure, costs, registration. Ich kann fragen, ob man in Raten zahlen kann. :: I can ask whether you can pay in instalments. Ich kann beim Waffelverkauf meine Hilfe anbieten. :: I can offer my help at the waffle sale."]]},{"u":"situation-mit-freunden.html","t":"Mit Freunden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Making plans with friends: a coffee, a barbecue, a birthday party."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann einen Freund oder eine Freundin einladen. :: I can invite a friend. Ich kann eine Einladung annehmen oder höflich absagen. :: I can accept an invitation or decline politely. Ich kann fragen, was ich mitbringen soll. :: I can ask what I should bring."]]},{"u":"situation-parken.html","t":"Parken","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann ein Halteverbot mit Zusatzzeichen verstehen. :: I can understand a no-stopping sign with an extra plate. Ich kann fragen, ob ich hier kurz halten darf. :: I can ask whether I may stop here for a moment. Ich kann verstehen, wo ich auf keinen Fall parken darf. :: I can understand where I must never park."]]},{"u":"situation-wanderung.html","t":"Wanderung","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann Warnschilder am Wanderweg und im Wald verstehen. :: I can understand warning signs on the trail and in the forest. Ich kann im Notfall die 112 anrufen und einen Rettungspunkt nennen. :: In an emergency I can call 112 and name a rescue point."]]},{"u":"situation-zu-hause.html","t":"Zu Hause","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Everyday life with the children: getting up, breakfast, homework, bedtime and house rules."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann die Kinder am Morgen wecken und sagen, was sie tun müssen. :: I can wake the children in the morning and tell them what to do. Ich kann fragen, wie es in der Schule war. :: I can ask how school was. Ich kann bei den Hausaufgaben helfen und einfache Regeln sagen. :: I can help with homework and state simple rules. Ich kann Gute Nacht sagen und eine kurze Geschichte vorlesen. :: I can say good night and read a short story aloud."]]},{"u":"situation-zugfahrt.html","t":"Zugfahrt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann auf der Anzeige im Zug lesen, wann und wo der Zug hält. :: I can read on the display in the train when and where the train stops. Ich kann den Halteknopf drücken, wenn der Zug nur bei Bedarf hält. :: I can press the stop button when the train only stops on request. Ich kann fragen, ob dieser Zug zum Hauptbahnhof fährt. :: I can ask whether this train goes to the main station."]]},{"u":"sofort.html","t":"sofort","s":"immediately","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich mache die Musik sofort leiser. :: I'll turn the music down right away."]]},{"u":"sohn.html","t":"Sohn","s":"son","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn spielt am Samstag Fußball. :: My son plays football on Saturday."]]},{"u":"sollen.html","t":"sollen","s":"should / to be supposed to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er soll um halb zehn da sein. :: He should be there at half past nine. Sollen wir etwas mitbringen? :: Should we bring something?"]]},{"u":"sondern.html","t":"sondern","s":"but (rather)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgen arbeite ich nicht im Büro, sondern von zu Hause. :: Tomorrow I'm not working in the office but from home."],["notes","Notes","After a negation, sondern gives the right alternative. Otherwise but is aber ."]]},{"u":"sonst.html","t":"sonst","s":"otherwise / else","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Beeil dich, sonst kommen wir zu spät. :: Hurry up, otherwise we'll be late."]]},{"u":"spaet.html","t":"spät","s":"late","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie spät ist es? :: What time is it?"]]},{"u":"spannend.html","t":"spannend","s":"exciting","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zehn zu zehn. Es ist sehr spannend! :: Ten all. It's very exciting!"]]},{"u":"spende.html","t":"Spende","s":"donation","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Auch über kleine Spenden freuen wir uns sehr. :: We are also very happy about small donations. Wir möchten nicht ausschließlich auf Spenden angewiesen sein. :: We don't want to depend only on donations."]]},{"u":"spiel.html","t":"Spiel","s":"match / game","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel. :: On Saturday we have a match."],["notes","Notes","Heimspiel : home match. Auswärtsspiel : away match."]]},{"u":"spielen.html","t":"spielen","s":"to play","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter spielt Handball. :: My daughter plays handball. Ihr habt gut gespielt. :: You played well."]]},{"u":"spielplan-der-handballmannschaft.html","t":"Spielplan der Handballmannschaft","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Spielplan der Mädchen, D-Jugend Match schedule of the girls, under-13 team Samstag, 14. November: Heimspiel um 11 Uhr in unserer Sporthalle. Saturday 14 November: home match at 11 o'clock in our sports hall. Sonntag, 22. November: Auswärtsspiel um 15 Uhr. Abfahrt mit dem Bus um 13:30 Uhr an der Halle. Sunday 22 November: away match at 3 pm. The bus leaves at 1.30 pm at the hall. Bitte seid immer 45 Minuten vor dem Spiel in der Halle. Please always be in the hall 45 minutes before the match. Beim Heimspiel verkaufen die Eltern Kuchen und Getränke. Wer backt einen Kuchen? At the home match the parents sell cake and drinks. Who will bake a cake? Bitte tragt euch in die Liste an der Tür ein. Please put your name on the list on the door."],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. Heimspiel : home match. Auswärtsspiel : away match. seid and tragt euch ein are commands to the players: the Imperativ with ihr ."]]},{"u":"spielverlegung-pokal-und-bezirksliga.html","t":"Nachricht des Trainers: zwei Spiele verlegt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo liebe Eltern! Hello, dear parents! Wetterbedingt konnten wir ja heute Nachmittag nicht spielen. Because of the weather we could not play this afternoon. Somit musste das Spiel verschoben werden. So the match had to be postponed. Hinzu kommt, dass wir am nächsten Samstag 22.08.26 unser erstes reguläres Bezirksligaspiel hätten. On top of that, next Saturday, 22.08.26, we would have our first regular Bezirksliga match. Am 22.08.26 ist aber das Schulfest am Gymnasium und hier sind 7 SpielerInnen von uns betroffen. But on 22.08.26 there is the school festival at the Gymnasium, and 7 of our players are affected. Somit haben wir für beide Spiele neue Termine, die euch bitte vormerken solltet: So we have new dates for both matches, which you should please note down: Pokalspiel (Termin alt 15.08.26): Verein A II gegen JSG B. Termin neu: Montag 17.08.26, 19.15 Uhr in Ort C. Treffen um 18.15 Uhr in Ort C! Cup match (old date 15.08.26): Club A II against JSG B. New date: Monday 17.08.26, 19:15 in Town C. Meeting at 18:15 in Town C! Bezirksligaspiel (Termin alt 22.08.26): Verein A II gegen JSG B. Termin neu: Sonntag 23.08.26, 11.00 Uhr, Kunstrasen in Ort D. Treffen um 10.00 Uhr in Ort D. League match (old date 22.08.26): Club A II against JSG B. New date: Sunday 23.08.26, 11:00, artificial pitch in Town D. Meeting at 10:00 in Town D. Beste Grüße Best regards"],["notes","Notes","Treffen is the time the players meet, usually one hour before Anpfiff (kick-off). Put the meeting time in the calendar, not the kick-off. die euch bitte vormerken solltet is a slip of the coach: correct is die ihr euch bitte vormerken solltet . vormerken is reflexive here (sich etwas vormerken). SpielerInnen with a capital I is a gender-neutral spelling: male and female players. musste verschoben werden is the passive with a modal verb: see the grammar entry Passiv mit werden ."]]},{"u":"sporttasche.html","t":"Sporttasche","s":"sports bag","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn hat seine Sporttasche zu Hause vergessen. :: My son forgot his sports bag at home."]]},{"u":"stark.html","t":"stark","s":"strong","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die andere Mannschaft ist sehr stark. :: The other team is very strong."]]},{"u":"termin-beim-kinderarzt.html","t":"Termin beim Kinderarzt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Arzthelferin: Kinderarztpraxis, guten Morgen. :: Paediatric practice, good morning. ich: Guten Morgen. Mein Sohn ist krank. Ich brauche heute einen Termin. :: Good morning. My son is ill. I need an appointment today. Arzthelferin: Was hat er denn? :: What's wrong with him? ich: Er hat seit gestern Fieber und Husten. :: He has had a fever and a cough since yesterday. Arzthelferin: Wie hoch ist das Fieber? :: How high is the fever? ich: Heute Morgen hatte er 39 Grad. :: This morning he had 39 degrees. Arzthelferin: Kommen Sie bitte um elf Uhr. Bringen Sie die Versichertenkarte mit. :: Please come at eleven o'clock. Bring the health insurance card. ich: Gut, um elf Uhr. Vielen Dank! :: Good, at eleven o'clock. Thank you very much!"],["variations","Variations","7 Arzthelferin: Heute ist leider alles voll. Kommen Sie morgen um acht in die offene Sprechstunde. :: Sadly everything is full today. Come to the open consultation tomorrow at eight."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Versichertenkarte (also Gesundheitskarte ): the card of the health insurance. Bring it every quarter, and the U-Heft for check-ups."]]},{"u":"termin.html","t":"Termin","s":"appointment","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich brauche heute einen Termin. :: I need an appointment today. Mein Sohn hat morgen einen Termin beim Kinderarzt. :: My son has an appointment at the paediatrician's tomorrow."],["notes","Notes","False friend: Termin is not a term ; it is an appointment with a fixed time."]]},{"u":"teuer.html","t":"teuer","s":"expensive","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Fußballschuhe sind leider sehr teuer. :: Unfortunately the football boots are very expensive."],["notes","Notes","The e drops before an ending: ein teures Trikot , teurer ."]]},{"u":"tochter.html","t":"Tochter","s":"daughter","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist krank und bleibt heute zu Hause. :: My daughter is ill and is staying at home today."]]},{"u":"tor.html","t":"Tor","s":"goal","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Your son scored two goals. Sie ist die Nummer sieben, im Tor. :: She is number seven, in goal."]]},{"u":"trainer.html","t":"Trainer","s":"coach","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bei anderen Fragen sprecht gerne eure Trainer an. :: For other questions, feel free to talk to your coaches. Ich schreibe dem Trainer eine Nachricht. :: I'm writing a message to the coach. Der Trainer schreibt alles in den Chat. :: The coach writes everything in the chat."],["false-friends","False friends","der Trainer is the coach, a person. Sports shoes are die Turnschuhe or die Sportschuhe , not Trainer ."]]},{"u":"trainieren.html","t":"trainieren","s":"to train","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Mannschaft trainiert am Dienstag und am Donnerstag. :: The team trains on Tuesday and Thursday."],["notes","Notes","Verbs ending in -ieren have no ge- in the Perfekt: trainiert ."]]},{"u":"training.html","t":"Training","s":"training, practice","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kind A. kann heute leider nicht zum Training kommen. :: Child A. sadly cannot come to training today. Das Training beginnt um 17.45 Uhr. :: Training starts at 5:45 pm. Beim nächsten Training ist er wieder dabei. :: He'll be there again at the next training. Wie war das Training heute? :: How was training today? Wegen Regen fällt das Training heute leider aus. :: Because of rain, training is cancelled today."],["pronunciation","Pronunciation","Said the English way: TRAI-ning , with a German r ."]]},{"u":"traurig.html","t":"traurig","s":"sad","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist traurig, weil das Training ausfällt. :: My son is sad because training is cancelled."]]},{"u":"treffen-verb.html","t":"treffen","s":"to meet","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir treffen uns um drei im Café. :: We meet at three in the café."],["notes","Notes","sich treffen : to meet each other. jemanden treffen : to meet someone."]]},{"u":"treffen.html","t":"Treffen","s":"meeting, meeting time","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Treffen um 18.15 Uhr in Ort C! :: Meeting at 18:15 in Town C! Das Treffen ist eine Stunde vor dem Anpfiff. :: The meeting is one hour before kick-off."],["notes","Notes","In a match message Treffen is when the players must be there, not when the match starts. The noun is the infinitive of sich treffen , so it is neuter."]]},{"u":"trennbare-verben.html","t":"Trennbare Verben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Some verbs have a prefix that splits off: anrufen, abholen, aufstehen, mitbringen . In a main clause the verb is in position 2 and the prefix goes to the end. Ich hole die Kinder um vier ab . Wann fängt das Training an ? With a modal verb, or after weil and dass , the verb stays together at the end: Ich muss die Kinder abholen. ..., weil das Training um vier anfängt. In the Perfekt, ge- goes between the prefix and the verb: abgeholt, angerufen, aufgestanden . The stress is always on the prefix: AB-holen ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Bei trennbaren Verben steht das Präfix am Satzende: Ich rufe dich an. Im Perfekt: Ich habe dich angerufen."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich abhole meine Tochter um vier. :: Ich hole meine Tochter um vier ab. Ich habe die Schule geanruft. :: Ich habe die Schule angerufen."]]},{"u":"treppenhaus.html","t":"Treppenhaus","s":"stairwell","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Treppenhaus hängt ein Zettel. :: There is a note hanging in the stairwell."]]},{"u":"trikot.html","t":"Trikot","s":"team shirt","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Trikot bekommt er von uns. :: He gets the shirt from us."]]},{"u":"trinken.html","t":"trinken","s":"to drink","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er soll viel trinken. :: He should drink a lot."]]},{"u":"trotzdem.html","t":"trotzdem","s":"anyway / nevertheless","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es regnet, trotzdem findet das Spiel statt. :: It's raining, but the match is taking place anyway."],["notes","Notes","After trotzdem at the start, the verb comes right away."]]},{"u":"tschuess.html","t":"tschüss","s":"bye","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bis morgen, tschüss! :: See you tomorrow, bye!"],["notes","Notes","Informal goodbye. Formal: Auf Wiedersehen ."]]},{"u":"ueber.html","t":"über","s":"over / above / about","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir sprechen über den Ausflug. :: We will talk about the trip. Das Bild hängt über dem Sofa. :: The picture hangs above the sofa."],["notes","Notes","über plus Akkusativ also means about : über den Ausflug sprechen ."]]},{"u":"ueberqueren.html","t":"überqueren","s":"to cross","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Überqueren Sie die Straße möglichst zügig und auf direktem Weg. :: Cross the road as quickly as possible and straight across. Die Kinder überqueren die Straße an der Ampel. :: The children cross the road at the traffic lights."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe die Straße geüberquert. :: Ich habe die Straße überquert."],["notes","Notes","über- is not separable here: ich überquere , participle without ge- . The sign also uses queren with the same meaning: Der Wanderweg quert hier eine Straße."]]},{"u":"ueberweisung.html","t":"Überweisung","s":"bank transfer","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Preis wird von jedem Mitfahrer selbst per Überweisung getätigt. :: Each participant pays the price themselves by bank transfer. Diese Überweisung gilt als verbindliche Anmeldung. :: This transfer counts as a binding registration."],["false-friends","False friends","At the doctor, die Überweisung is a referral to a specialist."]]},{"u":"uhrzeit-und-zeitangaben.html","t":"Uhrzeit und Zeitangaben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Clock time with um : um acht Uhr, um halb acht (7:30), um Viertel nach vier (4:15), um Viertel vor fünf (4:45). Days and parts of the day with am : am Montag, am Wochenende, am Nachmittag (but in der Nacht ). Months and seasons with im : im Dezember, im Sommer . From... to: von neun bis zwölf Uhr . By a day: bis Mittwoch . halb looks forward to the next hour: halb acht is 7:30, not 8:30."],["simple-german","Simple German","um acht Uhr, am Montag, im Dezember. halb acht = 7:30."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Am acht Uhr :: Um acht Uhr In Montag :: Am Montag"]]},{"u":"um.html","t":"um","s":"at (clock time) / around","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. :: We start at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"und.html","t":"und","s":"and","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie hat Fieber und bleibt heute zu Hause. :: She has a fever and is staying at home today."]]},{"u":"unser.html","t":"unser","s":"our","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist auf unserem Platz. :: The match is on our pitch."],["notes","Notes","Endings like ein ."]]},{"u":"unten.html","t":"unten","s":"downstairs / below","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir wohnen unten im Erdgeschoss. :: We live downstairs on the ground floor."]]},{"u":"unter.html","t":"unter","s":"under / below","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Schuhe stehen unter dem Bett. :: The shoes are under the bed."]]},{"u":"vater.html","t":"Vater","s":"father","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Vater holt die Kinder um vier Uhr ab. :: The father picks up the children at four o'clock."]]},{"u":"verabredung-am-wochenende.html","t":"Verabredung am Wochenende","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Freundin: Hey! Hast du am Samstag Zeit? :: Hey! Are you free on Saturday? ich: Am Vormittag nicht, da hat mein Sohn ein Spiel. Aber am Nachmittag habe ich Zeit. :: Not in the morning, my son has a match then. But in the afternoon I'm free. Freundin: Hast du Lust auf einen Kaffee in der Stadt? :: Do you fancy a coffee in town? ich: Ja, gern! Um wie viel Uhr? :: Yes, I'd love to! What time? Freundin: Um drei? Im Café am Marktplatz? :: At three? In the café on the market square? ich: Perfekt. Bis Samstag! :: Perfect. See you on Saturday!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Leider nicht, ich habe keine Zeit. Vielleicht nächste Woche? :: Sadly not, I'm not free. Maybe next week?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. da here means then : am Vormittag, da hat mein Sohn ein Spiel ."]]},{"u":"verb-an-position-2.html","t":"Verb an Position 2","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","In a German main clause the conjugated verb is always the second element. The first element can be the subject, a time or a place; when it is not the subject, the subject comes right after the verb. Ich / gehe morgen zum Training. Morgen / gehe ich zum Training. Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel. In yes-or-no questions and in commands the verb comes first: Kommst du mit? Komm bitte!"],["simple-german","Simple German","Im Hauptsatz steht das Verb auf Position 2. Heute spielt mein Sohn Fußball. Bei Ja-Nein-Fragen steht das Verb am Anfang."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Morgen ich gehe zum Training. :: Morgen gehe ich zum Training. Am Samstag wir haben ein Spiel. :: Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel."]]},{"u":"vergessen.html","t":"vergessen","s":"to forget","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe mein Heft vergessen. :: I forgot my exercise book."]]},{"u":"verlieren.html","t":"verlieren","s":"to lose","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schade, ihr habt verloren. :: Pity, you lost."]]},{"u":"verschieben.html","t":"verschieben","s":"to postpone, to move","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Somit musste das Spiel verschoben werden. :: So the match had to be postponed. Wir verschieben das Training auf Donnerstag. :: We are moving training to Thursday."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Das Spiel ist verschiebt. :: Das Spiel ist verschoben."],["notes","Notes","verlegen is used the same way: Das Spiel wurde verlegt. verschieben auf + Akkusativ gives the new date."]]},{"u":"verwendungszweck.html","t":"Verwendungszweck","s":"payment reference","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Verwendungszweck: Vorname und Nachname des Kindes und Spanien 2027. :: Payment reference: the child's first name and surname and \"Spanien 2027\". Bitte geben Sie die Rechnungsnummer als Verwendungszweck an. :: Please give the invoice number as the payment reference."],["notes","Notes","The field on a bank transfer that says what the money is for. Copy it exactly, or the club cannot match your payment."]]},{"u":"viel-spass.html","t":"Viel Spaß!","s":"Have fun!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Viel Spaß beim Feiern! :: Have fun celebrating! Viel Erfolg! :: Good luck! (with a task) Viel Glück! :: Good luck!"],["usage","Usage","beim plus a verb as a noun says what to have fun with: beim Spiel , beim Grillen ."]]},{"u":"viel.html","t":"viel","s":"much / a lot","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er soll viel trinken. :: He should drink a lot. Wir brauchen mehr Autos. :: We need more cars."],["notes","Notes","Before a noun: viel Zeit , viele Kinder ."]]},{"u":"vielleicht.html","t":"vielleicht","s":"maybe","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Vielleicht nächste Woche? :: Maybe next week?"]]},{"u":"vier.html","t":"vier","s":"four","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I'll pick her up at quarter past four."]]},{"u":"viertel.html","t":"Viertel","s":"quarter","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I will pick her up at quarter past four. Das Training fängt um Viertel vor fünf an. :: Training starts at quarter to five."]]},{"u":"voll.html","t":"voll","s":"full","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist leider alles voll. :: Sadly everything is full today."]]},{"u":"vollpension.html","t":"Vollpension","s":"full board","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Vollpension heißt Buffet am Morgen, Mittag und Abend. :: Full board means a buffet in the morning, at midday and in the evening. Das Hotel ist mit Vollpension im Preis inbegriffen. :: The hotel with full board is included in the price."],["notes","Notes","Halbpension is half board: breakfast and dinner."]]},{"u":"von.html","t":"von","s":"from / of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: That is very kind of you."]]},{"u":"vor.html","t":"vor","s":"in front of / before / ago","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid 45 Minuten vor dem Spiel in der Halle. :: Please be in the hall 45 minutes before the match. Ich warte vor der Halle auf dich. :: I'm waiting for you in front of the hall."],["notes","Notes","With time it always takes the Dativ: vor dem Spiel , vor zwei Jahren (two years ago)."]]},{"u":"vorlesen.html","t":"vorlesen","s":"to read aloud","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Liest du mir noch eine Geschichte vor? :: Will you read me a story?"]]},{"u":"vormerken.html","t":"vormerken","s":"to note down, to make a note of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir haben neue Termine, die ihr euch bitte vormerken solltet. :: We have new dates, which you should please note down. Ich merke mir den Termin vor. :: I'm making a note of the date."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich vormerke mir den Termin. :: Ich merke mir den Termin vor."],["notes","Notes","With a thing as object the reflexive pronoun is in the dative: ich merke mir etwas vor . Without sich it means to reserve or put on a list: Ich habe Sie für Montag vorgemerkt."]]},{"u":"w-fragen.html","t":"W-Fragen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Questions with a question word put the word first and the verb second. Wer? Was? Wann? Wo? Wohin? Woher? Wie? Warum? Wie viel? Um wie viel Uhr? Wann fängt das Training an? Wo ist das Spiel? Wer kann fahren? Was fehlt dir? Yes-or-no questions start with the verb: Hast du Zeit? Kommt ihr auch?"],["simple-german","Simple German","W-Frage: Fragewort, dann Verb: Wann kommst du? Ja-Nein-Frage: Verb am Anfang: Kommst du?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wann das Training fängt an? :: Wann fängt das Training an? Wo du wohnst? :: Wo wohnst du?"]]},{"u":"waehrend.html","t":"während","s":"during","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Während des Spiels sitzen die Eltern auf der Tribüne. :: During the match the parents sit on the stand."]]},{"u":"waermepumpe.html","t":"Wärmepumpe","s":"heat pump","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Firma A finanziert Ihnen den Kauf der Wärmepumpe über einen Ratenkauf. :: Company A finances your purchase of the heat pump through a hire purchase. Sie zahlen erst nach Installation der Wärmepumpe. :: You only pay after the heat pump has been installed. Unsere alte Ölheizung wird durch eine Wärmepumpe ersetzt. :: Our old oil heating is being replaced by a heat pump."],["notes","Notes","A compound noun takes the article of its last part: die Wärme + die Pumpe = die Wärmepumpe ."]]},{"u":"wann.html","t":"wann","s":"when","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wann fängt das Training an? :: When does training start? Weißt du, wann er anfängt? :: Do you know when it starts?"],["notes","Notes","wann asks for a time. For when in a statement, use wenn or als ."]]},{"u":"warm.html","t":"warm","s":"warm","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Kinder brauchen warme Kleidung. :: The children need warm clothes. Von neun bis zwölf Uhr gibt es kein warmes Wasser. :: From nine to twelve there is no hot water."],["notes","Notes","warmes Wasser is hot water from the tap."]]},{"u":"warten.html","t":"warten","s":"to wait","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich warte vor der Halle auf dich. :: I am waiting for you in front of the hall."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich warte für dich. :: Ich warte auf dich."]]},{"u":"warum.html","t":"warum","s":"why","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ja, warum? :: Yes, why?"],["notes","Notes","The answer often starts with weil ."]]},{"u":"was-fehlt-dir.html","t":"Was fehlt dir?","s":"What's wrong with you?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Was fehlt Ihnen? :: What's wrong with you? (Sie) Was hat er denn? :: What's wrong with him?"],["usage","Usage","The doctor's question. The answer often uses wehtun : Mein Hals tut weh."]]},{"u":"was-gibts.html","t":"Was gibt's?","s":"What's up? / What is it?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ja, bitte. Was gibt's? :: Yes, please. What is it? Was gibt's Neues? :: What's new?"],["usage","Usage","When someone wants to talk to you. gibt's is gibt es ."]]},{"u":"was.html","t":"was","s":"what","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast? Was fehlt dir denn? :: What's wrong with you?"],["notes","Notes","In speech was also means something : Träum was Schönes!"]]},{"u":"waschen.html","t":"waschen","s":"to wash","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wer wäscht diese Woche die Trikots? :: Who is washing the team shirts this week?"]]},{"u":"wechselpraepositionen.html","t":"Wechselpräpositionen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","in, an, auf, unter, über, vor, hinter, neben, zwischen take two cases. Wohin? (where to, movement) takes the Akkusativ: Wir gehen in die Halle. Ich lege den Ball auf den Tisch. Wo? (where, place) takes the Dativ: Wir sind in der Halle. Der Ball liegt auf dem Tisch. Short forms: ins = in das , im = in dem , am = an dem . Ins Bett gehen but im Bett liegen ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Wohin? Akkusativ: in die Schule . Wo? Dativ: in der Schule ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wir gehen in der Halle. :: Wir gehen in die Halle. Ich bin in die Schule. :: Ich bin in der Schule."]]},{"u":"wegen.html","t":"wegen","s":"because of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wegen Regen fällt das Training heute leider aus. :: Because of rain, training is cancelled today."],["notes","Notes","In writing with the Genitiv: wegen des Regens . In speech often with the Dativ, or with no article."]]},{"u":"wehtun.html","t":"wehtun","s":"to hurt","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Hals tut weh. :: My throat hurts."],["notes","Notes","Mir tut der Bauch weh : my tummy hurts. The person who feels the pain is in the Dativ."]]},{"u":"weil.html","t":"weil","s":"because","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich rufe an, weil meine Tochter krank ist. :: I am calling because my daughter is ill."],["notes","Notes","After weil the conjugated verb goes to the end: weil sie krank . ist"]]},{"u":"weit.html","t":"weit","s":"far / wide","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ist die Halle weit von hier? :: Is the hall far from here?"]]},{"u":"welcher.html","t":"welcher","s":"which","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Welche Schuhe brauchst du? :: Which shoes do you need?"],["notes","Notes","Endings like der, die, das : welcher, welche, welches ."]]},{"u":"wenig.html","t":"wenig","s":"little / not much","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe heute wenig Zeit. :: I have little time today."]]},{"u":"wenn-es-sich-einrichten-laesst.html","t":"wenn es sich einrichten lässt","s":"if it can be arranged, if possible","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Hallo, wenn es sich einrichten lässt, ja. :: Hello, if it can be arranged, yes. Ich komme, wenn es sich einrichten lässt. :: I'll come if I can make it work."],["usage","Usage","A polite yes with a condition: you would like it, but you understand it may not always work. wenn möglich is shorter."]]},{"u":"wenn.html","t":"wenn","s":"if / when","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte rufen Sie wieder an, wenn sie länger krank ist. :: Please call again if she is ill for longer."]]},{"u":"wer.html","t":"wer","s":"who","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wer kann fahren? :: Who can drive? Wen rufst du an? :: Who are you calling?"]]},{"u":"wichtig.html","t":"wichtig","s":"important","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Versichertenkarte ist sehr wichtig. :: The health insurance card is very important."]]},{"u":"widerrufen.html","t":"widerrufen","s":"to withdraw, to revoke","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Käufer kann seine Vertragserklärung innerhalb von 14 Tagen ohne Angabe von Gründen widerrufen. :: The buyer can withdraw his contractual declaration within 14 days without giving reasons. Hiermit widerrufe ich den abgeschlossenen Vertrag. :: I hereby withdraw from the contract I concluded. Die Vollmacht bleibt bis zu ihrem Widerruf gültig. :: The power of attorney stays valid until it is revoked."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich rufe den Vertrag wider. :: Ich widerrufe den Vertrag. Ich habe den Vertrag gewiderrufen. :: Ich habe den Vertrag widerrufen."],["notes","Notes","wider- (against) is not separated here, so the participle has no ge- . Do not mix it up with wieder (again). The noun is der Widerruf , the period is the Widerrufsfrist ."]]},{"u":"wie-gehts.html","t":"Wie geht's?","s":"How are you?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wie geht es dir? :: How are you? (du) Wie geht es Ihnen? :: How are you? (Sie)"],["usage","Usage","The everyday question when you meet someone you know. Germans expect a real, short answer."]]},{"u":"wie-spaet-ist-es.html","t":"Wie spät ist es?","s":"What time is it?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wie viel Uhr ist es? :: What time is it? Es ist halb acht. :: It's half past seven."],["usage","Usage","Both questions mean the same."]]},{"u":"wie-steht-es.html","t":"Wie steht es?","s":"What's the score?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Zwölf zu zehn für uns. :: Twelve to ten for us. Es steht unentschieden. :: It's a draw."],["usage","Usage","On the stand during a match. The score is said with zu : drei zu eins ."]]},{"u":"wie-wars-in-der-schule.html","t":"Wie war's in der Schule?","s":"How was school?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wie war das Training? :: How was training? Wie war dein Wochenende? :: How was your weekend?"],["usage","Usage","The question when a child comes home. war's is war es ."]]},{"u":"wie.html","t":"wie","s":"how","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie war das Training heute? :: How was training today? Um wie viel Uhr? :: What time?"],["notes","Notes","wie viel : how much. wie viele : how many. so groß wie : as big as."]]},{"u":"wieder.html","t":"wieder","s":"again","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte rufen Sie wieder an. :: Please call again."]]},{"u":"wir.html","t":"wir","s":"we","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Nachbarn laden uns zum Grillen ein. :: Our neighbours invite us to a barbecue."]]},{"u":"wirklich.html","t":"wirklich","s":"really","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wirklich? Das freut mich! :: Really? I'm glad!"]]},{"u":"wissen.html","t":"wissen","s":"to know (a fact)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich weiß es noch nicht. :: I don't know yet."],["notes","Notes","wissen is for facts; kennen is for people and places."]]},{"u":"wo.html","t":"wo","s":"where","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wann und wo ist das Spiel? :: When and where is the match?"],["notes","Notes","wo? asks for a place: Dativ after in, an, auf ."]]},{"u":"wochenende.html","t":"Wochenende","s":"weekend","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie war dein Wochenende? :: How was your weekend?"]]},{"u":"woher.html","t":"woher","s":"where from","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Woher kommen Sie? :: Where are you from?"]]},{"u":"wohin.html","t":"wohin","s":"where to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wohin fahrt ihr am Wochenende? :: Where are you going at the weekend?"],["notes","Notes","wohin? asks for a direction: Akkusativ after in, an, auf ."]]},{"u":"wohnen.html","t":"wohnen","s":"to live (somewhere)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich wohne im zweiten Stock. :: I live on the second floor."],["notes","Notes","wohnen is where you live; leben is to be alive, or to live in a country."]]},{"u":"wohnung.html","t":"Wohnung","s":"flat / apartment","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Wohnung ist im Erdgeschoss. :: Our flat is on the ground floor."]]},{"u":"wollen.html","t":"wollen","s":"to want","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich will zuerst spielen. :: I want to play first."],["notes","Notes","Ich will sounds direct. To ask politely, say Ich möchte ."]]},{"u":"zaehne-putzen.html","t":"Zähne putzen","s":"to brush one's teeth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Putz bitte die Zähne! :: Please brush your teeth! Hast du die Zähne geputzt? :: Have you brushed your teeth?"],["usage","Usage","German says die Zähne putzen , the teeth, not my teeth ."]]},{"u":"zahlen.html","t":"Zahlen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","0 null, 1 eins, 2 zwei, 3 drei, 4 vier, 5 fünf, 6 sechs, 7 sieben, 8 acht, 9 neun, 10 zehn, 11 elf, 12 zwölf From 13 to 19: number plus -zehn : dreizehn, vierzehn , but sechzehn and siebzehn . From 21 the units come first: einundzwanzig (21), fünfunddreißig (35). Tens: zwanzig, dreißig, vierzig, fünfzig, sechzig, siebzig, achtzig, neunzig, hundert . Ordinals for dates and floors: der erste, zweite, dritte, vierte , then -te up to 19 and -ste from 20. am 19. November is read am neunzehnten November ."],["simple-german","Simple German","21 ist einundzwanzig : zuerst die Eins, dann die Zwanzig. Ordinalzahlen: erste, zweite, dritte ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","zwanzigeins :: einundzwanzig der dreite Stock :: der dritte Stock"]]},{"u":"zahn.html","t":"Zahn","s":"tooth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Putz bitte noch schnell die Zähne. :: Please quickly brush your teeth."]]},{"u":"zehn.html","t":"zehn","s":"ten","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: May I watch TV for ten more minutes?"]]},{"u":"zeit-haben.html","t":"Zeit haben","s":"to have time / to be free","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Hast du am Samstag Zeit? :: Are you free on Saturday? Haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Do you have a moment? Ich habe leider keine Zeit. :: Sadly I'm not free."],["usage","Usage","To ask whether someone is free. No time is keine Zeit , not nicht Zeit ."]]},{"u":"zeit.html","t":"Zeit","s":"time","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du am Samstag Zeit? :: Do you have time on Saturday? Ich habe leider keine Zeit. :: Sadly I have no time."]]},{"u":"zettel-im-treppenhaus.html","t":"Zettel im Treppenhaus","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Liebe Nachbarn, Dear neighbours, am Samstag ab neun Uhr kommen die Handwerker. Sie reparieren die Heizung im Keller. On Saturday from nine o'clock the workmen are coming. They will repair the heating in the basement. Von neun bis zwölf Uhr gibt es kein warmes Wasser. From nine to twelve there will be no hot water. Bitte stellen Sie keine Fahrräder und Kinderwagen vor die Kellertür. Please do not put bicycles or prams in front of the basement door. Vielen Dank für Ihr Verständnis! Thank you for your understanding! Ihre Hausverwaltung Your property management"],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. Hausverwaltung : the company that looks after the building for the owner. Nothing to answer: keep the hall in front of the basement free on Saturday."]]},{"u":"zettel.html","t":"Zettel","s":"note / slip of paper","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie ihm einen kurzen Zettel mit. :: Please give him a short note to take."]]},{"u":"zimmer.html","t":"Zimmer","s":"room","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Räum bitte dein Zimmer auf! :: Please tidy up your room!"]]},{"u":"zu-hause-bleiben.html","t":"zu Hause bleiben","s":"to stay at home","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sie bleibt heute zu Hause. :: She is staying at home today. Er soll drei Tage zu Hause bleiben. :: He should stay at home for three days."],["usage","Usage","zu Hause : at home. nach Hause : home, where to."]]},{"u":"zu-laut.html","t":"Zu laut","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, es ist schon elf Uhr. Könnten Sie bitte die Musik leiser machen? :: Excuse me, it's already eleven o'clock. Could you please turn the music down? Nachbar: Oh, Entschuldigung! Ist es so laut? :: Oh, sorry! Is it that loud? ich: Ja, leider. Meine Kinder können nicht schlafen. :: Yes, unfortunately. My children can't sleep. Nachbar: Das tut mir leid. Ich mache sie sofort leiser. :: I'm sorry. I'll turn it down right away. ich: Danke, das ist nett. Gute Nacht! :: Thanks, that's kind. Good night!"],["variations","Variations","4 Nachbar: Wir feiern heute. Es dauert nur noch eine halbe Stunde. :: We're celebrating today. It will only go on for another half hour."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Könnten Sie bitte ...? is the polite way to ask. From ten in the evening the house rules ask for quiet ( Nachtruhe )."]]},{"u":"zu.html","t":"zu","s":"to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: We are going to the paediatrician today."],["notes","Notes","zum is zu dem , zur is zu der . zu Hause means at home."]]},{"u":"zuerst.html","t":"zuerst","s":"first","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play."]]},{"u":"zufahrt.html","t":"Zufahrt","s":"access road","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Feuerwehrzufahrt muss immer frei bleiben. :: The fire brigade access must always stay clear. Die Zufahrt zum Parkplatz ist heute gesperrt. :: The access to the car park is closed today."],["notes","Notes","A car parked in a Feuerwehrzufahrt is towed away ( abgeschleppt ). Einfahrt is the way in, Ausfahrt the way out; Einfahrt freihalten on a garage door means: do not block it."]]},{"u":"zusammen.html","t":"zusammen","s":"together","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir frühstücken am Sonntag zusammen. :: We have breakfast together on Sunday."],["notes","Notes","Hallo zusammen! greets a whole group."]]},{"u":"zwanzig.html","t":"zwanzig","s":"twenty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","In der Klasse sind zwanzig Kinder. :: There are twenty children in the class."],["notes","Notes","Tens and units are said backwards: 21 is einundzwanzig , one-and-twenty."]]},{"u":"zwei.html","t":"zwei","s":"two","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Your son scored two goals."],["notes","Notes","On the phone people often say zwo so it is not confused with drei ."]]},{"u":"zweite.html","t":"zweite","s":"second","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich wohne im zweiten Stock. :: I live on the second floor."]]},{"u":"zwischen.html","t":"zwischen","s":"between","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Café ist zwischen der Bank und dem Supermarkt. :: The café is between the bank and the supermarket."]]},{"u":"zwoelf.html","t":"zwölf","s":"twelve","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zwölf zu zehn für uns. :: Twelve to ten for us."]]}];
